{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; git status --short; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_alu.py\n# Shared radix-4 combinational divider\n\nImplemented a single unsigned magnitude divider in `rtl/alu.sv`, shared by\nDIV, DIVU, REM and REMU. Sixteen generated combinational digits consume the\ndividend from its most significant pair. D, 2D and 3D are 34 bits; each\ndigit computes three independent 35-bit unsigned differences and uses\ntheir borrow bits to select digit 3, 2, 1 or 0 and its remainder.\nSigned operations convert inputs to magnitudes and conditionally negate\nthe final quotient/remainder. Output overrides implement division by zero;\nINT_MIN/-1 naturally yields INT_MIN and remainder zero. No native division\nor remainder operators remain in the real RTL. The multiplier, base ALU,\nALTOPS expressions, core interfaces and pipeline were preserved.\n\nThe implementation follows the hypothesis. Stage-local remainder signals\navoid Verilator's false circular-dependency warning on unpacked arrays;\nquotients grow by two bits per digit and reach 32 bits at the final digit.\nTests retain the existing suite and add an independent integer RV32M\noracle, full boundary cross-products, divisor-multiple boundaries,\nall radix-4 quotient digits/positions, deterministic random operand pairs,\nall sign combinations and random zero divisors.\n\nLocal validation:\n\n- `make lint TARGET=bench`: PASS, no warnings. The literal wildcard lint\n  command encounters the baseline's source-order issue (`core.sv` precedes\n  the typedefs in `core_pkg.sv`); the repository lint target supplies\n  `core_pkg.sv` first as required by its documentation.\n- `make test TARGET=bench`: PASS (all five unit suites, including all 27\n  ALU tests). The three added division tests check 70,428 RTL results\n  across DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU against the independent integer oracle.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=8 bash formal/run_all.sh`:\n  PASS: 53 checks passed, zero failed, first attempt. Automatic nret=1\n  wrapper/config selection preserved the declared RVFI contract. No\n  counterexamples or formal fix attempts. The ALTOPS expression block\n  was also compared byte-for-byte with HEAD and is unchanged.\n- `make timing TARGET=bench`: PASS. Gowin option 0: 5.350 MHz, 154 logic\n  levels, 6,681 logic cells, 460 registers. Worst arrival: 192.228 ns,\n  from MEM/WB rd through register-file bypass, EX and the ALU to EX/MEM.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: PASS (both selftest and CoreMark).\n  Selftest retirement traces passed with and without both bus stalls;\n  CoreMark passed the existing stalled-bus CRC, UART and bounds checks.\n- `NRET=1 make fpga TARGET=bench`: PASS for all three Gowin placement\n  options and the scored CoreMark run. Fmax values: 5.350, 5.627, 5.627 MHz;\n  median 5.627 MHz, fitness 12.53 iterations/second. CoreMark: 10 iterations,\n  4,491,485 cycles between its MMIO timing markers.\n\nRelative to the supplied baseline (5.442 MHz, 12,312 logic cells), measured\nmedian Fmax improves by approximately 3.4% and logic usage falls by 45.7%.\nThe divider remains the critical combinational path; reducing the number\nof digits did not halve its delay. Option 0 alone is slower than the\nbaseline median, but the evaluator scores the median of all three options.\n\nThe normal formal gate uses ALTOPS and does not prove the real arithmetic;\nthe expanded cocotb vectors and cosim exercise the real divider. Full\n`formal-deep` was not run because the repository documents that real\nM-extension SMT checks can exceed this implementation's 30-minute budget.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
