and taken rule locally, and feeds a four-way selection. Each bank computes\nits own training match and saturating update. Payload arrays use Gowin's\nsyn_ramstyle=\"distributed_ram\" attribute. Reset clears validity only.\n\nThe algorithm, EX advance/recovery/training events, accepted prediction\nsnapshots, two-entry queue, five stages, complete ID/EX operand registers,\nexplicit flop register file and real/ALTOPS MUL/DIV implementations are\nunchanged. There is no deferred update or write-through bypass. No\nevaluation-contract, benchmark, decoder \n…[4195 of 7267 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:278f293065a7955e]…\nnance RAM at 19068), generated/netlist_mapping.log and unchanged-flow\ngenerated/timing/gowin_p{0,1,2}/impl/pnr/core_bench.tr.\n\nThe only deviation from separate payload declarations is packing metadata:\nthe initial separate counter arrays became 128 flops despite the attribute,\nso they did not satisfy the required payload mapping. That intermediate\nversion measured 80.417 MHz median / 198.083 iter/sec and passed all checks,\nbut was not retained. Packing preserves every bit and policy while forcing\nthe requested RAM16 topology. Local training read ports replicate shallow\nRAM storage during inference;\nthe logical predictor capacity and all tag/target bits remain unchanged.\nRouting, remaining EX recovery and divider paths now limit timing. No\nunrelated datapath changes were introduced to chase the acceptance margin.\n\nScratch verification artifacts live in cores/bench/generated/ and are\ngitignored. This implementation note is the explicitly requested exception\nto the source/test edit scope and is also gitignored.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
