{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_77", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; git status --short; cmp cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-wvLtcFzCe/if_stage.sv; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'", "aggregated_output": " M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_if_stage.py\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n# Eight-bank next-PC table\n\n## Implementation\n\nOnly `rtl/if_stage.sv` changes architecturally. The 64-entry logical table\nis implemented by eight generate scopes, each owning eight-word native tag,\naligned target, conditional-kind and counter arrays and an eight-bit valid\nvector. Fetch and training use PC[7:5] for bank and PC[4:2] for row. Every\nbank compares its asynchronous row tag against all of fetch PC[31:8]. A\ncomplete eight-way case selects the hit, target, kind and two-bit counter.\n\nEach bank qualifies the original training event with its bank ID. Its\ntraining match reads its own pre-edge validity/tag. Allocation, weak\ninitialization, changed-kind initialization, saturating updates and matching\ninvalidation retain the original policy. Reset clears validity independently\nof bank selection and leaves payload memories unreset. No bypass or delayed\ntraining was added. Fetch queue, EX recovery, M units, handshakes, retirement\nand the nret=1 interface are unchanged.\n\n## Tests\n\n`test_if_stage.py` adds a flat 64-entry predictor reference and an independent\nFIFO/PC reference. Directed checks cover all 64 indices, each of the 24 tag\nbits, all eight counter transitions, replacements, both changed kinds,\nmatching/nonmatching invalidation, high targets, reset priority and all\nsame-row lookup/training bank pairs. Random traffic checks disabled events,\nindependent fetch/decode holds, full queue replacement, correction and reset.\nEvery valid selected payload and prediction is checked before/after edges.\nThe original queue regression remains intact.\n\n`test_pipeline.py` retains existing predictor, FIFO, operand and retirement\nassertions and adds repeated jump chains through all bank/row combinations,\nwith independent imem/dmem stalls, dependent load-to-branch, accepted MUL and\nDIVU responses, wrong-path stores, exact PC streams and once-only bus effects.\n\n## Local validation\n\n- Verilator lint: passes with no warnings.\n-\n…[1115 of 4187 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:80623301ace40bf1]…\n8/70.398 MHz, median 70.398 MHz; 6,421 logic cells, 1,793\n  registers, 216 LUT-RAM, four BSRAM, two DSP. At unchanged bracketed cycles,\n  fitness is 173.404 iterations/sec. This is below the approximately\n  81.162 MHz / 199.922 iterations/sec acceptance thresholds.\n- An equivalent bank-local one-hot/OR mux was also tested. Its three\n  placements measured 65.949/68.321/68.321 MHz and 6,461 logic cells, so it\n  was discarded. The final source retains the better complete-case mux.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\nNo policy or pipeline deviation. Lookup uses an explicit complete case to\nkeep all selected fields together; storage remains eight independently\nwritten shallow banks. The layout removes all three predictor BSRAMs but\nloses Fmax. The supplied 78.372 MHz option-0 probe was not reproduced.\nOption 0's worst path goes through EX, IF and ID; options 1/2's worst paths\ngo through EX and decode operand delivery. Native shallow-memory mapping\ntherefore succeeded, but the measured fitness hypothesis is a regression.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
