{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_42", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; git status --short --untracked-files=all; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'", "aggregated_output": " M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_ex_stage.py\n# Parallel carry-consistency prediction verification\n\nChanged only `rtl/ex_stage.sv` and added coverage in `test/test_ex_stage.py`.\nThe three EX match bits now use a combinational function deriving required\ncarries directly from prediction XOR operands, checking each adjacent local\ncarry relation independently, and reducing 32 agreement bits through an\nexplicit 32/16/8/4/2/1 AND tree. The function contains no sum, subtraction,\nripple carry, or sequential state. Only carry out of bit 31 is omitted.\nJALR forces the required carry into bit zero to zero, independently checks\nprediction bit zero, and retains the original operands' bit-zero carry.\n\nThe architectural PC+4, PC+immediate and rs1+immediate adders remain intact.\nOutcome/legality/alignment selection, redirect and training qualification,\nEX/MEM payloads, forwarding, blocking M transactions, predictor table and\nqueue, pipeline schedule and nret=1 RVFI ports are unchanged. No evaluation\nsource, formal configuration, bound or checker was edited.\n\nAdded independent Python integer-addition checks of all three match outputs:\nexhaustive three-bit operand/prediction windows at every bit position with\nboth carry-in possibilities; edge and alternating patterns; every individual\nprediction-bit corruption; every carry-run start/length; signed-looking\nimmediates; wraparound; deterministic full-width random triples; direct and\nsequential coincidence; stale ordinary/illegal/misaligned predictions;\nJALR's four operand low-bit combinations, both prediction low bits and all\nthree standalone forwarding sources. Existing branch/ALU/M, saved-response,\nhold, reset and pipeline assertions are retained.\n\nFinal local validation:\n- Exact requested Verilator lint command: PASS, no warnings.\n- `make bench` and `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: PASS for all five ELFs,\n  including unstalled/stalled reference traces and canonical stalled CoreMark.\n- Unchanged CoreMark evaluation helper: completed, ten iterations in exactly\n…[1406 of 4478 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c80598bfaef9f45b]…\n557 MHz champion.\n  This hypothesis does not meet the acceptance threshold.\n  The reported worst setup paths include the unchanged divider and the\n  architectural ALU/decode bypass cones. Reports are under\n  `cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p{0,1,2}/impl/pnr/core_bench.tr`.\n\nDeviation: the reusable local function stores only the 31 generated carries\nthat are checked; the unobserved carry out of bit 31 is never computed.\nThere is no target, PC, operand or comparison truncation. Notes are kept in\nthe explicitly permitted `cores/bench/implementation_notes.md` location.\n\nConcern: correctness and unchanged cycle count do not establish a fitness\nimprovement. Vendor mapping and the independent architectural target adders\nor unchanged divider may limit Fmax. Acceptance at this cycle count requires\nmedian Fmax above about 85.309 MHz and fitness above 210.131 iterations/sec.\nThe measured result is a regression, so the predicted six percent improvement\nis not supported by this implementation's vendor timing results.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
