{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'import json; from pathlib import Path; b=json.loads(Path(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\").read_text().splitlines()[0]); new=5.393*1000000*10/4208674; old=b[\\\"fmax_mhz\\\"]*1000000*b[\\\"iterations\\\"]/b[\\\"cycles\\\"]; print(json.dumps({\\\"baseline_fitness\\\":old,\\\"new_fitness\\\":new,\\\"fitness_gain_pct\\\":100*(new/old-1),\\\"cycles_saved_pct\\\":100*(1-4208674/b[\\\"cycles\\\"]),\\\"ipc_gain_pct\\\":100*(b[\\\"cycles\\\"]/4208674-1),\\\"fmax_change_pct\\\":100*(5.393/b[\\\"fmax_mhz\\\"]-1)},indent=2))'; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"baseline_fitness\": 12.116259989736134,\n  \"new_fitness\": 12.814012204318985,\n  \"fitness_gain_pct\": 5.758808536412441,\n  \"cycles_saved_pct\": 6.296603461883987,\n  \"ipc_gain_pct\": 6.719717421686733,\n  \"fmax_change_pct\": -0.9004042631385545\n}\nImplemented the specified 32-entry direct-mapped next-PC predictor in IF,\nindexed by PC[6:2] with full PC[31:7] tags, aligned targets, a conditional\nbit and two-bit saturating counters. Only valid bits reset. Prediction\nmetadata travels through IF/ID and ID/EX; EX resolves and compares every\nvalid instruction. Correctly predicted transfers retain the target fetch.\nRecovery and training occur only on valid EX advance, and correction wins\nover instruction-bus and load-use stalls while respecting data-bus freeze.\nRVFI retains resolved next-PC and the unchanged nret=1 top-level contract.\n\nTraining uses a compact internal packed bundle with split PC index/tag and\nan aligned target. A control=false update invalidates only a matching tag;\nthis represents ordinary/illegal instructions and faulty control targets.\nUntaken branches with misaligned targets also invalidate a matching entry\nwithout trapping, preserving architectural behavior while avoiding invalid\ntarget storage. No additional predictor or EX-to-IF bypass was introduced.\n\nDirected cocotb scenarios check branch loops and both direction errors,\ntag collisions/replacement, stale ordinary/load/illegal entries, alternating\nJALR targets (including bit-zero clearing), aligned and misaligned JAL,\nJALR and taken/untaken branches. They run with zero-wait, instruction\nbackpressure, three-cycle data waits, and combined stalls. Checks include\nexact PC/instruction retirement, resolved RVFI PC, sequential order,\narchitectural trap/writeback, and every accepted bus store. They also\ncheck training/recovery suppression and complete PC/ID-EX hold during\ndata stalls, plus one-cycle target retirement after warm taken branches.\n\nLocal validation so far:\n- Verilator -Wall lint: pass, no warnings.\n- Existing decoder, ALU, immediate, register-file and pipeline tests: pass.\n- Single-channel formal: pass, 53 checks, 0 failures on the first run;\n  no counterexample and no fix attempts required.\n- Selftest cosim with and without random stalls, and stalled CoreMark\n  canonical CRC validation: pass (make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1).\n- Stalled CoreMark timing-marker validation: pass, 10 iterations in\n  4,208,674 bracketed cycles, 2.376045281720561e-6 iterations/cycle.\n- Gowin option 0 timing: 5.107 MHz, 141 levels, 12,928 logic cells,\n  589 registers, 52 LUT-RAM, 6 BSRAM and 6 DSP. Worst paths still cross\n  forwarding and the existing combinational ALU.\n- Median three-option FPGA evaluation is running; final results will\n  be added when complete.\n\nConcern: option 0 Fmax is lower than the recorded 5.442 MHz baseline;\nthe acceptance gain depends on the measured median and cycle reduction.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
