{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n print(d['id'],d.get('category'),d.get('outcome'),d.get('fitness'),d.get('fmax_mhz'),d.get('cycles'),d['title'])\n if d.get('category')=='micro_opt' and 'baseline' not in d['id']:\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  if isinstance(h,dict): print('PROPOSAL:',h.get('hypothesis',''))\n  print('PATH:',d.get('critical_path'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-bc10e33 micro_opt improvement 12.12 5.442 4491485 Baseline retest for cores/bench\nhyp-20260930-001-r1s0 micro_opt regression 12.53 5.627 4491485 Shared radix-4 combinational divider for RV32M\nPROPOSAL: Replace only the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU logic in alu.sv with a shared,\npurely combinational unsigned radix-4 divider that produces quotient and\nremainder together. Retain the existing ALU interface, multiplier, base\noperations, and exact RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitutions.\n\nFor signed operations, form unsigned magnitudes of the two operands and\nremember quotient sign = a[31] XOR b[31] and remainder sign = a[31]. For\nunsigned operations, use the operands directly. Precompute zero-extended\nD, 2D and 3D in 34 bits, with no truncation of 3D. Unroll 16 radix-4 digits\nfrom the dividend's most significant pair to its least significant pair.\nStarting with R=0, each digit forms T=(R<<2)|next_pair in 34 bits, computes\nT-D, T-2D and T-3D concurrently using 35-bit unsigned subtractions, and\nuses their borrow bits to select the largest valid digit 3, 2, 1 or 0.\nSelect the corresponding remainder and append that two-bit quotient\ndigit. Use subtraction borrow bits directly, avoiding a separate bank\nof comparators followed by subtractors. The selected R fits in 32 bits\nbecause R<D for every nonzero divisor. Feed the final magnitude quotient\nor remainder through the appropriate conditional two's-com