{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_54", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-001-r12s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20260930-001-r12s0\ntitle: \"Collapse serial divider digits into one parallel radix-16 step\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 200.89 iter/sec at median 81.557 MHz and 4,059,766\n  bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its worst reported path starts at divider\n  quotient_q[30] and ends at response_magnitude_q[5], taking 17.757 ns\n  through 67 cells. The real divider computes two dependent radix-4\n  digits per clock: the first subtraction and remainder selection feed\n  another full-width subtraction and selection. Earlier radix-4 and\n  LUT-factored launch-seed experiments removed other divider bottlenecks,\n  but did not eliminate this serial recurrence. The recent balanced\n  branch/SLT comparator improvement exposes it again. A local arithmetic\n  replacement can shorten it without adding any execution cycles.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace only the real divider's two serial radix-4 digit calculations\n  with one exact radix-16 digit calculation per existing iteration.\n  Preserve the four-bit launch seed, request capture, seven iteration\n  edges, registered magnitude/sign response, response transfer and\n  held-response behavior. This is one micro-optimization of the divider\n  recurrence, with no pipeline, predictor, bus or instruction-latency change.\n\n  At the existing request edge capture full-width unsigned divisor\n  multiples M[k]=k*D for k=1..15 in 36 bits. Produce these constants\n  with shifts and parallel add/subtract logic, using a carry-save\n  reduction before one carry-propagate adder for three-term constants;\n  do not build a serial chain M[k]=M[k-1]+D or infer general multipliers.\n  For example 7D=(D<<3)-D and 15D=(D<<4)-D. All magnitude and multiple\n  arithmetic must retain sufficient width for D=0xffffffff. The existing\n  launch seed and quotient/remainder initialization remain exact.\n\n  Each iteration forms the 36-bit trial T={remainder_q,quotient_q[31:28]}.\n  Compute fifteen 37-bit differences diff[k]={1'b0,T}-{1'b0,M[k]}\n  concurrently. Set ge[k]=!diff[k][36], deriving eligibility directly\n \n…[3353 of 6425 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c88e1f644b8be9a6]…\nmine success; no gain is claimed as measured yet.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 10\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/divider.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace the two dependent radix-4 steps with one parallel radix-16\n      step, captured 36-bit divisor multiples, 37-bit borrow-producing\n      trial differences, adjacent-eligibility one-hot selection and\n      balanced remainder/digit OR trees. Preserve the launch seed,\n      seven iteration clocks, sign/zero semantics, reset, handshake,\n      response registers and exact ALTOPS branch.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Retain independent RV32M result and existing transaction assertions.\n      Replace removed first_step signal checks with the equivalent\n      four-bit boundary comparison, retain the independent two-radix-4\n      reference, and extend directed vectors to cover all sixteen digits\n      and large-multiple borrow boundaries. Preserve every latency,\n      captured-input, held-response, reset and ALTOPS check.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
