ifteen candidate\n  differences {1'b0,T}-{1'b0,multiple_q[k]} concurrently in 37 bits. Let\n  ge[k] be the inverse of each difference's borrow bit, with ge[0]=1.\n  Select exactly one digit using sel[0]=!ge[1],\n  sel[k]=ge[k] && !ge[k+1] for k=1..14, and sel[15]=ge[15]. These are\n\n…[2204 of 5276 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a911304bea0bcb0f]…\ntapath with fifteen\n      parallel 37-bit trial subtractions, adjacent-borrow one-hot digit\n      selection and balanced masked-OR remainder selection. Capture\n      36-bit divisor multiples using shared balanced constant shift/add\n      logic on the existing launch edge. Preserve the eight-iteration\n      counter, all external ports, sign and zero-divisor handling,\n      final-edge result transfer, response holding, reset behavior and\n      the existing ALTOPS branch and transaction timing.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Extend existing division coverage with operands exercising every\n      quotient nibble, divisor-multiple boundaries including 36-bit\n      carries, divisors near 0x80000000 and 0xffffffff, all sign choices,\n      zero divisors and INT_MIN/-1. Compare to independent integer RV32M\n      semantics. Retain all current arithmetic, eight-iteration latency,\n      captured-operand, final-edge transfer, backpressure, reset and\n      ALTOPS checks without relaxing any assertions.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
