nding remainder and append that two-bit quotient\ndigit. Use subtraction borrow bits directly, avoiding a separate bank\nof comparators followed by subtractors. The selected R fits in 32 bits\nbecause R<D for every nonzero divisor. Feed the final magnitude quotient\nor remainder through the appropriate conditional two's-complement sign\ncorrection and select it by the ALU operation.\n\nHandle divisor zero explicitly at the output: quotient is 0xffffffff,\nremainder is the original dividend. Preserve DIV INT_MIN/-1 = INT_MIN\nand REM INT_MIN/-1 = 0, either through the magnitude algorithm or exact\noverrides. Do not use native / or % in the real synthesized divider.\nThis local arithmetic substitution reduces the \n…[14627 of 17699 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8745f1d0c83f95d3]…\nder launch are the main limitations.\n\nNOTES: \ncritical_path {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_2_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider/remainder_q_3_s1', 'slack_ns': -15.36, 'arrival_ns': 25.654, 'logic_cells': 26, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider']}\nhyp-20260930-002-r4s1 structural Registered shared multiplier removes multiplication from fast EX fitness 125.26 fmax 54.927 cycles 4384920\ncritical_path {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider/remainder_q_1_s1', 'slack_ns': -13.607, 'arrival_ns': 23.901, 'logic_cells': 24, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider']}\nhyp-20260930-003-r4s2 predictor Precompute predictor recovery candidates before execute fitness 125.16 fmax 52.536 cycles 4197517\ncritical_path {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -14.899, 'arrival_ns': 25.193, 'logic_cells': 13, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
