{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md schemas/hypothesis.schema.json'", "aggregated_output": "- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-001-r1s0 (regression, +3.38%): Halving the combinational divider's digit count left a serial borrow-driven subtraction/priority-mux chain on Gowin's critical path, so shared DIV/REM reduced LUT4s by 45.7% but gained only 3.4% Fmax at unchanged CoreMark cycles.\n- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-002-r1s1 (improvement, +609.08%): Replacing combinational `/` and `%` with a registered eight-iteration divider capped at four restoring steps per clock shortened the EX critical path enough for the Fmax gain to outweigh CoreMark's extra divide cycles.\n- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-003-r1s2 (regression, +5.69%): The 32-entry tagged next-PC predictor cut stalled CoreMark cycles by 6.3%, but the forwarding/combinational DIV/REM path still limited Fmax to 5.393 MHz, so removing control-flow bubbles could not match the registered-divider design.\n- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-002-r2s1 (improvement, +20.29%): Two radix-4 digits per iteration with parallel D/2D/3D subtraction and a response register before sign correction shorten the divider-to-EX/MEM path, while a four-bit launch seed preserves nine-clock EX latency.\n- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-002-r3s1 (regression, +7.87%): Squashing only ID/EX valid while capturing raw imem_data independently of flush removes late branch-to-decode/operand feedback and raised prototype Fmax 7.87% at unchanged CoreMark cycles; load-use holds must use imem_ready rather than redirect-masked fetch validity to keep redirect out of payload enables.\n- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-003-r3s2 (improvement, +13.90%): Pairing 64-entry tagged next-PC prediction with the retimed divider and validity-only ID/EX recovery converts CoreMark's taken-transfer bubble savings into a throughput gain by keeping redirect out of instruction decode and payload capture enables.\n- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-002-r4s1 (improvement, +6.38%): Registering forwarded operands and one shared unsigned 32x32 product before carry-save signed-high correction removes multiplication from the fast ALU mux, letting the clock gain outweigh CoreMark's added MUL stalls.\n- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-001-r5s0 (regression, +5.31%): Factoring the four-bit divider launch seed into LUT4 truth masks and a balanced OR tree removes serial subtract/priority selection at unchanged CoreMark cycles, exposing the ordinary ALU-to-dmem address path as the next Fmax bottleneck.\n- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-003-r5s2 (improvement, +6.16%): A two-entry fall-through IF queue improves stalled CoreMark by fetching ahead on the predicted path during load-use, dmem, and MUL/DIV holds and delivering queued instructions while raw imemReady is low.\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\