{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_33", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-001-r6s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20260930-001-r6s0\ntitle: \"Operand-local divider seed bypasses full-width signed magnitude carry\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 132.98 iter/sec at 53.987 MHz and 4,059,766\n  bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its worst reported Gowin path runs from\n  register-file data through ID and EX to divider remainder initialization:\n  24.550 ns through 22 cells. The earlier LUT-factored seed reached\n  57.843 MHz on the preceding champion, but retained a full 32-bit\n  conditional negation before seed lookup and exposed another EX path.\n  The magnitude/seed retiming attempt regressed. Optimize this launch\n  cone locally, preserving all division clocks and the new fetch queue.\nhypothesis: |\n  Compute the four-bit divider launch seed directly from the original\n  forwarded operands instead of routing it through full-width absolute\n  values. This is one combinational divider-initialization optimization;\n  preserve capture, seven iterations, registered response and transfer,\n  all handshake behavior, pipeline stages, prediction, and nret=1.\n\n  Let neg_a = signed_op && a[31] and neg_b = signed_op && b[31].\n  Derive the absolute dividend's high nibble N locally. For neg_a=0,\n  N=a[31:28]. For neg_a=1, N=(~a[31:28] + (a[27:0]==0)) modulo 16.\n  The lower-bit zero reduction supplies the carry into bit 28 without\n  waiting for a 32-bit two's-complement carry chain. Independently derive\n  the absolute divisor's low nibble d as neg_b ? -b[3:0] : b[3:0], with\n  explicitly four-bit arithmetic. Detect magnitude below 16 directly:\n  small_d = neg_b ? ((b[31:4]==28'hfffffff) && (b[3:0]!=0))\n                 : (b[31:4]==0).\n  The negative case recognizes exactly -15 through -1; -16 must take the\n  large-divisor bypass. Unsigned values with the top bit set remain large.\n\n  Replace the two serial narrow subtract/select seed digits with a\n  factored, combinational LUT4 truth-mask function seed4(N,d). For\n  d=1..15 it returns {N modulo d, floor(N/d)} in two four-bit fields;\n  for d=0 it returns {N,4'hf}. Generate its 16-by\n…[2167 of 5239 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:be9b7bab1930014a]…\nr-recovery paths\n  and lookup fanout/routing may cap the gain below the 4.6 percent gate.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/divider.sv\n    description: |\n      Derive the seed dividend prefix, divisor nibble and small-divisor\n      classification directly from original request operands using narrow\n      arithmetic and balanced reductions. Replace serial small_seed\n      arithmetic with offline-generated LUT4 truth masks and balanced\n      selection. Preserve quotient-tail magnitude, divisor multiples,\n      iteration datapath, all transaction timing and ALTOPS behavior.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Add independent checks for prefix carry from zero/nonzero lower\n      bits, all seed nibble pairs, signed and unsigned divisor bypass\n      boundaries, extreme operands and randomized RV32M results. Retain\n      exact latency, captured-input, response-hold, reset and ALTOPS\n      assertions; use unchanged pipeline, formal and CoreMark gates.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
