{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_27", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id']=='hyp-20260930-003-r4s2':\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis']);print(d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Keep the existing 64-entry tagged target/direction predictor unchanged.\nChange only how its exact prediction is verified and how operand-\nindependent recovery PCs reach EX. In ID, compute sequential_candidate\n= fetch PC + 4 and direct_candidate = fetch PC + the existing decoded\nimmediate, using full 32-bit modulo arithmetic. Compare the fetch's\nexisting predicted_next_pc against each candidate with full-width\nequalities. Register both candidates and both one-bit equality results\nwith the instruction in ID/EX. Retain predicted_next_pc for the dynamic\nJALR target comparison. This adds no pipeline stage, no predictor state,\nand no prediction or recovery cycle; the experiment is early prediction\nverification, rather than a new direction or target predictor.\n\nUse these ID/EX field names and order after predicted_next_pc to match\nthe measured prototype: predicted_sequential_target[31:0],\npredicted_direct_target[31:0], prediction_sequential_match, and\nprediction_direct_match. Capture all four under the same reset-or-\n!stall payload update rule as PC, instruction, immediate, and prediction.\nPreserve validity-only flushes, with flush taking priority over holds\nfor valid alone. Do not gate the raw instruction, decoder, register-file\naddresses, or payload enables with redirect. Bubbles may retain decoded\nfields; existing stage-valid qualification must continue to isolate them.\n\nIn EX, replace in.pc + 4 with the registered sequential candidate and\nreplace in.pc + in.imm with the registered direct candidate for branch\nand JAL target resolution, target alignment checks, predictor training,\ncorrective redirect targets, architectural pc_next, and jump link data.\nReplace the current sequential_match and direct_match comparators with\ntheir registered equality bits. Keep the full forwarded rs1 + immediate\nJALR calculation, bit-zero clearing, alignment check, and comparison\nagainst saved predicted_next_pc in EX. Select the appropriate one-bit\nmatch using the actual branch outcome and existing legality/trap rules.\nOrdinary, illegal, \n…[1506 of 4578 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:79ec5a5779bd1377]…\n taken/not-taken\nrepair, changing JALR targets, stale prediction repair for noncontrol and\nillegal instructions, and misaligned branch/jump traps. Exercise load-to-\nbranch dependencies and imem/dmem/divider holds, checking exact retired\nPCs, resolved RVFI next PCs, link values, contiguous order, and absence\nof wrong-path stores. Retain the unchanged decoder/ALU suites, formal\ngates, and stalled CoreMark canonical CRC/UART/marker checks.\n\nThe forecast is a 6 percent fitness gain at unchanged CoreMark cycles,\nsupported by the prototype's 6.3 percent median Fmax improvement. At\n4,197,517 cycles, Fmax must exceed approximately 51.70 MHz to beat the\nchampion by 4.6 percent. The main risks are shifting a critical path into\nID and changed placement when the final implementation differs from the\nprototype. The remaining multiplier/forwarding path still limits timing;\ndo not alter it within this predictor hypothesis. Re-evaluate all three\nvendor placement options and the full correctness gates after implementation.\n\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\nroot=Path('cores/bench/generated/jalr_probe')\nrtl=root/'rtl';rtl.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\nfor p in Path('cores/bench/rtl').glob('*.sv'):\n shutil.copy2(p,rtl/p.name)\np=rtl/'ex_stage.sv';s=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('  always_comb begin\\\\n    case (in.ctrl.branch_op)', '''  // Four byte slices calculate carry-0/carry-1 sums in parallel.\n  logic [8:0] j0, j10, j11, j20, j21, j30, j31;\n  logic jp1, jp2;\n  logic jc1, jc2, jc3;\n  logic jm0, jm10, jm11, jm20, jm21, jm30, jm31;\n  assign j0 = {1'b0, rs1[7:0]} + {1'b0, in.imm[7:0]};\n  assign j10 = {1'b0, rs1[15:8]} + {1'b0, in.imm[15:8]};\n  assign j11 = {1'b0, rs1[15:8]} + {1'b0, in.imm[15:8]} + 9'd1;\n  assign j20 = {1'b0, rs1[23:16]} + {1'b0, in.imm[23:16]};\n  assign j21 = {1'b0, rs1[23:16]} + {1'b0, in.imm[23:16]} + 9'd1;\n  assign j30 = {1'b0, rs1[31:24]} + {1'b0, in.imm[31:24]};\n  assign j31 = {1'b0, rs1[31:24]} + {1'b0, in.imm[31:24]} + 9'd1;\n  assign jp1 = &(rs1[15:8] \"'^ in.imm[15:8]);\n  assign jp2 = &(rs1[23:16] ''^ in.imm[23:16]);\n  assign jc1 = j0[8];\n  assign jc2 = j10[8] | (jp1 & j0[8]);\n  assign jc3 = j20[8] | (jp2 & j10[8]) | (jp2 & jp1 & j0[8]);\n  assign jalr_sum = {jc3 ? j31[7:0] : j30[7:0],\n                     jc2 ? j21[7:0] : j20[7:0],\n                     jc1 ? j11[7:0] : j10[7:0], j0[7:0]};\n  assign jm0 = (in.predicted_next_pc[7:0] == {j0[7:1], 1'\"'b0});\n  assign jm10 = (in.predicted_next_pc[15:8] == j10[7:0]);\n  assign jm11 = (in.predicted_next_pc[15:8] == j11[7:0]);\n  assign jm20 = (in.predicted_next_pc[23:16] == j20[7:0]);\n  assign jm21 = (in.predicted_next_pc[23:16] == j21[7:0]);\n  assign jm30 = (in.predicted_next_pc[31:24] == j30[7:0]);\n  assign jm31 = (in.predicted_next_pc[31:24] == j31[7:0]);\n  assign jalr_match = jm0 & (jc1 ? jm11 : jm10)\n                         & (jc2 ? jm21 : jm20)\n                         & (jc3 ? jm31 : jm30);\n\n  always_comb begin\n    case (in.ctrl.branch_op)''')\ns=s.replace('    jalr_sum    = rs1 + in.imm;\\\\n','')\ns=s.replace(\\\"  assign jalr_match = (in.predicted_next_pc == {jalr_sum[31:1], 1'b0});\\\\n\\\",'')\np.write_text(s)\nprint(rtl)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
