{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_33", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-001-r8s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20260930-001-r8s0',\n 'title':'Parallel carry-select JALR target and prediction verification',\n 'category':'micro_opt',\n 'motivation':'''The champion scores 177.66 at median 72.124 MHz and 4,059,766 bracketed CoreMark cycles. A fresh unchanged Gowin placement-0 run reproduced 68.145 MHz. Its detailed worst paths reveal EX/MEM validity qualifying forwarded rs1, a long JALR carry chain, prediction comparison, and corrective fetch-address selection. The tag/target table endpoints are their fetch-address inputs, not evidence of a training-memory bottleneck. Nearly equal paths reach the target table and fetch PC itself. Shortening JALR target verification can therefore address their common cone. Earlier one-hot operand routing regressed, delayed training regressed, and delayed recovery failed liveness; preserve their current timing and use a local arithmetic/comparison change.''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Replace only EX's rs1-plus-immediate JALR target and prediction-match datapath with four 8-bit carry-select slices and parallel per-slice equality checks. Keep the actual forwarded operand sources, pipeline registers, predictor policy, queue, immediate correction, training and every instruction latency unchanged. This is one combinational micro-optimization, not a new prediction feature or recovery stage.\n\nFor byte zero calculate the exact 9-bit zero-extended sum s0={0,rs1[7:0]}+{0,imm[7:0]}. For each upper byte i=1,2,3 calculate in parallel 9-bit sums si0=ai+bi and si1=ai+bi+1, retaining the overflow bits. Define gi=si0[8] and pi=AND(ai XOR bi). Resolve the entering carries with group lookahead: c1=s0[8], c2=g1 OR (p1 AND c1), and c3=g2 OR (p2 AND g1) OR (p2 AND p1 AND c1). Assemble jalr_sum from s0[7:0] and each upper byte's carry-selected low eight sum bits. All arithmetic remains modulo 2\"'^32, including negative sign-extended immediates and address wrap. Keep the independently computed real target {jalr_sum[31:1],1'\"'b0} for redirects, training and architectural next-PC reporting.\n\nIn parallel with group-carry resolution compare saved predicted_next_pc against both sum candidates within each upper byte. Byte-zero match compares predicted_next_pc[7:0] with {s0[7:1],1'b0}, preserving the JALR bit-zero rule and requiring prediction bit zero to be zero. Select each upper byte's one-bit match with its entering carry, then AND the four byte matches. Thus high-byte equality reduction begins before the carry-selected full target word exists, removing the serial full-width adder, word selection and 32-bit equality reduction from redirect control. Preserve the complete 32-bit equality, including high address bits; never compare only the benchmark address range or use the predicted PC as the architectural target.\n\nRetain JALR's existing target-bit-one misalignment trap, suppressed link write and sequential fallback on trap, decoder legality, branch/JAL/sequential match behavior, valid-qualified EX advance, exact once-per-advance training and immediate redirect. Preserve both forwarding sources and retained invalid-WB history, dmem/MUL/DIV holds, response payloads, validity-only decode flush, all reset priorities, every queue occupancy/acceptance rule, old-data predictor lookup, nret=1 ports and contiguous RVFI retirement order. No new registers or arithmetic request timing are needed, and the real and ALTOPS M-extension paths remain intact.\n\nValidate this combinational circuit against an independent native 32-bit add and cleared-bit target equality for arbitrary operands and predictions. Directed EX tests should exercise carry generation, propagation and kill across every byte boundary, all-ones runs, negative immediates, modulo wrap, matching and one-bit-different predictions in every byte, all operand/prediction low-bit choices, high-bit-only mismatches, both forwarding routes, alignment traps, stalls and invalid/illegal instructions. Pipeline tests retain load-to-JALR, changing indirect targets, queued saved predictions, wrong-path side effects, both bus stalls and MUL/DIV response interactions. Run unchanged nret=1 formal and reference cosim gates and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/address-bound/timing-marker checks.\n\nThe expected benefit is Fmax at unchanged 4,059,766 bracketed cycles. Four short carry chains, group-carry logic and speculative byte matches cost modest extra add/comparator LUTs; Gowin may merge equivalent arithmetic or expose another ALU/divider path. Confirm a real circuit and median vendor timing improvement across placement options 0/1/2. At unchanged cycles the acceptance threshold is 75.442 MHz, more than 4.6 percent above the current 72.124 MHz champion. Forecast ten percent fitness improvement, subject to implementation-phase correctness, area and timing evaluation.''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':10,'confidence':'medium'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Replace the monolithic JALR addition and post-add full-word prediction comparator with exact byte-sliced carry-select sums, three group-lookahead carry signals, and parallel carry-selected byte equality bits. Continue to produce and use the independently resolved full-width real target. Preserve every existing alignment, legality, forwarding, advance, hold, redirect, training, payload and pipeline behavior.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_ex_stage.py','description':'''Extend the direct EX suite with independent 32-bit target and prediction-match expectations covering every carry boundary, propagate/kill patterns, wrap, signed immediates, bit-zero clearing, alignment traps, upper-bit mismatches, all forwarding sources and blocked/invalid/illegal events. Keep all existing MUL/DIV and response assertions.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain every existing pipeline assertion and add indirect-target sequences covering forwarded/load-fed JALR, changing targets and byte-boundary carry behavior during queued fetches, bus stalls and arithmetic holds. Check architectural PCs, links, traps, exact training/correction events, order and absence of wrong-path memory effects.'''}\n ]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=86))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Refined hypothesis is schema valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
