{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nfrom tools.eval.gowin import build_all,summarize\nwt=Path.cwd();root=wt/'cores/bench/generated/carry_check_probe'\nr=build_all(wt,root/'rtl','fpga/core_bench_si.sv',root/'timing')\n(root/'timing_result.json').write_text(json.dumps({'runs':r,'summary':summarize(r)},indent=2))\nprint(json.dumps(summarize(r),indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"placement_failed\": false,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 71.863,\n  \"seeds\": [\n    66.353,\n    71.863,\n    71.863\n  ],\n  \"perturbations\": [\n    [\n      0,\n      66.353,\n      16\n    ],\n    [\n      1,\n      71.863,\n      17\n    ],\n    [\n      2,\n      71.863,\n      17\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"lut4\": 4970,\n  \"ff\": 1925,\n  \"lutram\": 24,\n  \"bsram\": 7,\n  \"dsp\": 2,\n  \"logic_levels\": 16,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.ctrl.reg_write_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/target_q_target_q_0_0_s\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -10.071,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 20.365,\n    \"logic_cells\": 39,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_if\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_if\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_47", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-001-r8s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Parallel carry-consistency checking for JALR prediction verification'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 177.66 at median 72.124 MHz and 4,059,766 bracketed CoreMark cycles. A fresh unchanged Gowin placement-0 run reproduced 68.145 MHz. Its detailed worst paths reveal EX/MEM validity qualifying forwarded rs1, a JALR carry chain, prediction equality, and corrective fetch-address selection. The tag/target endpoints are fetch-address inputs; nearly equal paths reach the fetch PC itself. Earlier one-hot operand routing and delayed training regressed, and delayed recovery failed liveness. In this research turn, byte-sliced carry-select arithmetic reduced logic depth but placement 0 regressed to 67.434 MHz. Moving inverse-target arithmetic into ID regressed median timing to 56.213 MHz. The promising remaining local angle is to remove carry propagation only from prediction verification without changing the target adder or moving arithmetic across a stage.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Replace only the JALR prediction-match comparator in ex_stage.sv with a parallel local carry-consistency check. Keep the existing full 32-bit rs1+immediate adder and cleared-bit real target, every pipeline register, operand source, predictor entry and policy, immediate redirect/training timing, queue and arithmetic latency. This is one combinational micro-optimization: verify the predicted sum without waiting for the real sum's carry chain.\n\nLet A be the actual forwarded rs1, B the existing immediate, and P the exact saved predicted_next_pc. Compute bitwise propagate X=A XOR B and generate G=A AND B. For significant bits i=1..31 infer the only carry-in consistent with the predicted sum bit: C[i]=X[i] XOR P[i]. A JALR prediction matches exactly iff P[0]=0, C[1]=G[0], and every i=1..30 satisfies C[i+1]=G[i] OR (X[i] AND C[i]). Implement the thirty latter constraints as one vector equality, C[31:2] == (G[30:1] | (X[30:1] & C[30:1])), combined with the two low-bit conditions. Each bit's constraint is independent combinational logic and the reduction is balanced. Do not implement this as a serial carry recurrence. The identity follows by induction from the genuine zero carry into bit zero; carry-out of bit 31 is discarded because addition is modulo 2\"'^32.\n\nBit zero of the actual sum is intentionally ignored because JALR clears it, but its carry into bit one is still A[0] AND B[0]. Requiring P[0]=0 preserves complete equality to {jalr_sum[31:1],1'\"'b0}; all 31 higher predicted bits participate. No address bits may be narrowed to the benchmark range. Retain native jalr_sum=A+B for redirect_target, predictor training, alignment checking and architectural pc_next. Never substitute a predicted target for the real target. The verification and target arithmetic now settle in parallel instead of a full-width equality waiting behind the adder.\n\nPreserve the existing misaligned-JALR target-bit-one trap, link-write suppression and sequential fallback, decoder legality, branch/JAL/sequential match behavior, EX advance qualification, once-per-advance training and immediate correction. Preserve both forwarding paths and retained WB history, dmem/MUL/DIV holds and responses, payload capture, validity-only decode flush, reset priorities, queue acceptance/flush rules, saved immutable predictions, nret=1 interfaces and contiguous RVFI order. No new state, recovery cycle or change to real/ALTOPS M-extension arithmetic is required.\n\nProve or independently test equivalence of this Boolean matcher to P == ((A+B) & 0xfffffffe) for arbitrary full-width A, B and P. Cover carry generation/propagation/kill across every bit and byte boundary, all-ones runs, negative immediates, modulo wrap, correct and one-bit-different predictions at all 32 positions, all low-bit choices, upper-address-only mismatches, every forwarding route, misalignment traps, stalls and invalid/illegal instructions. Retain load-to-JALR, changing indirect targets, queued predictions, wrong-path side-effect and arithmetic-response tests. Run the unchanged nret=1 formal and reference cosim gates and canonical CRC/UART/bounds/marker-validated CoreMark.\n\nExpected CoreMark cycles remain 4,059,766; gains come entirely from Fmax. The extra bitwise carry checks are a modest LUT cost with no additional FFs. Gowin synthesis may factor the equations differently, and real-target selection, ordinary ALU or divider timing can cap the benefit. Confirm median vendor timing across placement options 0/1/2 and do not claim the score from a single placement. At unchanged cycles, median Fmax must exceed 75.442 MHz to clear the champion by more than 4.6 percent. Forecast eight percent improvement pending this exact circuit's vendor timing and implementation-phase correctness gates.'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'}\nd['changes']=[\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Replace only jalr_match's post-adder equality with the exact parallel propagate/generate and inferred-carry vector constraints described above. Preserve the native real-target sum, full address width, bit-zero clearing, alignment checks, every operand source, pipeline register, hold, redirect, training and payload behavior.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_ex_stage.py','description':'''Add independent full-width native-add/cleared-target expectations for random operands and predictions, all carry boundaries, propagate/kill patterns, wrap, signed immediates, all low-bit cases, upper-bit mismatches, forwarding choices, alignment traps and blocked/invalid/illegal events. Keep all existing MUL/DIV and response assertions.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain all current correctness checks and exercise forwarded/load-fed JALR with changing targets, carry-boundary behavior, queued saved predictions, bus stalls and arithmetic holds. Check actual PCs, links, traps, exact correction/training events, retirement order and absence of wrong-path side effects.'''}]\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=86))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final-angle hypothesis schema valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
