{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_13", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ['hyp-20260930-001-r6s0','hyp-20260930-001-r7s0','hyp-20260930-001-r4s0']:\n  print(d['id'],d['title']); print(d.get('hypothesis'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20260930-001-r4s0 One shared sign-extended DSP multiplier for all RV32M products\n{'motivation': 'The current champion scores 117.75 at 49.426 MHz and 4,197,517\\nbracketed CoreMark cycles. Its ALU describes separate signed-signed,\\nunsigned-unsigned, and signed-unsigned full products. All recent\\nimplementations use six DSP blocks. The prior micro_opt experiments\\naddressed division or recovery; none tested multiplier sharing.\\nA fresh Gowin placement-option-0 run on the unchanged champion\\nreproduced 46.008 MHz and the 27.030 ns worst path. Cell-level timing\\nexplicitly crosses u_alu/mul_ss_63_s0, including 3.760 ns inside its\\nDSP and substantial source fanout, routing, and result selection.\\nMultiplication is therefore a measured timing target after the\\nsuccessful registered-divider and validity-only recovery changes.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"Replace the three real combinational multiply expressions with ONE\\nshared signed 33x33 multiplication, using operation-dependent sign\\nextension on its inputs. Keep every multiplication at the existing\\nsingle-cycle EX latency. This is one local arithmetic-sharing micro-\\noptimization: retain the champion pipeline, predictor, divider,\\nforwarding, bus stalls, retirement width, and architectural results.\\n\\nDefine a_signed = (op == ALU_MULH || op == ALU_MULHSU) and\\nb_signed = (op == ALU_MULH). Form signed 33-bit operands\\nmul_a = $signed({a_signed && a[31], a}) and\\nmul_b = $signed({b_signed && b[31], b}). Compute an explicitly signed\\n66-bit product = mul_a * mul_b. MUL returns product[31:0]; MULH,\\nMULHU, and MULHSU all return product[63:32]. A zero leading bit\\nrepresents every unsigned 32-bit source as positive; the leading\\noperand sign bit represents signed sources exactly. The 66-bit\\nintermediate also represents unsigned products above 2^63 without\\ntreating them as negative. Do not use 32-bit signed casts, discard\\ncarry into bit 32, or apply serial post-multiply sign corrections.\\nMUL deliberately uses unsigned inputs since its low 32 bits are\\nidentical for all \n…[15087 of 18159 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e8418c4bf44399bf]…\nVFI.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Replace encoded case muxes with flat masked-OR rs1/rs2 selection.\\nBuild ALU operands directly from original forwarding candidates,\\nfolding PC/immediate selection into their enables to avoid a second\\nwide mux layer. Keep architectural source values and arithmetic\\nsaved payloads exact under every stall and forwarding choice.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_ex_stage.py', 'description': 'Adapt direct EX stimulus to the documented one-hot selector bits\\nwhile preserving existing expectations. Check every source route,\\nALU immediate and AUIPC operands, branch/JALR and store sources,\\nand MUL/DIV request capture without relaxing existing assertions.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Preserve current end-to-end checks and exercise simultaneous\\nEX/MEM and MEM/WB matches, x0, immediate false-source matches and\\nretained invalid-WB forwarding across multi-cycle dmem stalls.\\nRequire exact RVFI operands/results/order and exactly-once stores.\\n'}]}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
