{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\":\\\\s*\\\"structural\\\"|hyp-20260930-002-r9s1|hyp-20260930-002-r8s1|hyp-20260930-002-r7s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260930-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Move division out of the combinational execute path\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The only recorded bench experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12,\\nmedian Fmax 5.442 MHz, and a 199.837 ns path through forwarding and\\nu_ex/u_alu with 156 cells. No LESSONS.md or earlier structural attempts\\nexist in this fixture. The ALU implements signed and unsigned division\\nand remainder with combinational / and % operators. These are likely\\nresponsible for the very deep arithmetic path; even instructions that\\ndo not divide must meet the clock constraint imposed by that hardware.\\nMoving this arithmetic behind registers should substantially improve\\nFmax, at the cost of additional cycles only for DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only recorded bench experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12,\\nmedian Fmax 5.442 MHz, and a 199.837 ns path through forwarding and\\nu_ex/u_alu with 156 cells. No LESSONS.md or earlier structural attempts\\nexist in this fixture. The ALU implements signed and unsigned division\\nand remainder with combinational / and % operators. These are likely\\nresponsible for the very deep arithmetic path; even instructions that\\ndo not divide must meet the clock constraint imposed by that hardware.\\nMoving this arithmetic behind registers should substantially improve\\nFmax, at the cost of additional cycles only for DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational divide/remainder cone with one shared,\\nblocking, registered divider in EX. Use unsigned restoring division\\nwith four explicitly bounded quotient-bit steps per clock, eight\\niteration clocks, operand magnitude capture at launch, and signed\\ncorrection on completion. Target at most ten EX clocks from accepting\\na request to transferring its result under zero-wait memory, and at\\nmost ten clocks between successive retirements for back-to-back divide\\ninstructions. This keeps progress inside the existing formal liveness\\nwindow without changing any checker. Each\n…[98254 of 101326 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7280c38b8170de3a]…\ntness\": 191.13, \"delta_pct\": 7.58, \"vs_baseline\": 1476.98, \"fmax_mhz\": 77.593, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4059766, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4925, \"ff\": 1921, \"seeds\": [76.0, 77.593, 77.593], \"perturbations\": [[0, 76.0, 15], [1, 77.593, 14], [2, 77.593, 14]], \"lutram\": 24, \"bsram\": 7, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_val_0_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -8.158, \"arrival_ns\": 18.452, \"logic_cells\": 40, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 15, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-30T20:01:19.997303Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 9, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-002-r9s1 (improvement, +7.58%): Moving complete operand bypass selection before ID/EX removes late muxes from EX arithmetic and control paths, improving Fmax at unchanged CoreMark cycles provided EX loads wait for MEM data and MUL/DIV consumers capture accepted saved responses.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
