{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ['hyp-20260930-003-r4s2','hyp-20260930-002-r7s1']:\n  h=d['hypothesis']\n  print(d['id'], '\\\\n',h['hypothesis'] if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20260930-003-r4s2 \n Keep the existing 64-entry tagged target/direction predictor unchanged.\nChange only how its exact prediction is verified and how operand-\nindependent recovery PCs reach EX. In ID, compute sequential_candidate\n= fetch PC + 4 and direct_candidate = fetch PC + the existing decoded\nimmediate, using full 32-bit modulo arithmetic. Compare the fetch's\nexisting predicted_next_pc against each candidate with full-width\nequalities. Register both candidates and both one-bit equality results\nwith the instruction in ID/EX. Retain predicted_next_pc for the dynamic\nJALR target comparison. This adds no pipeline stage, no predictor state,\nand no prediction or recovery cycle; the experiment is early prediction\nverification, rather than a new direction or target predictor.\n\nUse these ID/EX field names and order after predicted_next_pc to match\nthe measured prototype: predicted_sequential_target[31:0],\npredicted_direct_target[31:0], prediction_sequential_match, and\nprediction_direct_match. Capture all four under the same reset-or-\n!stall payload update rule as PC, instruction, immediate, and prediction.\nPreserve validity-only flushes, with flush taking priority over holds\nfor valid alone. Do not gate the raw instruction, decoder, register-file\naddresses, or payload enables with redirect. Bubbles may retain decoded\nfields; existing stage-valid qualification must continue to isolate them.\n\nIn EX, replace in.pc + 4 with the registered sequential candidate and\nreplace in.pc + in.imm with the registered direct candidate for branch\nand JAL target resolution, target alignment checks, predictor training,\ncorrective redirect targets, architectural pc_next, and jump link data.\nReplace the current sequential_match and direct_match comparators with\ntheir registered equality bits. Keep the full forwarded rs1 + immediate\nJALR calculation, bit-zero clearing, alignment check, and comparison\nagainst saved predicted_next_pc in EX. Select the appropriate one-bit\nmatch using the actual branch outcome and existing legality/trap ru\n…[8085 of 11157 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:553360960ea37fbf]…\nsion\nretirement check. Do not change arithmetic, predictor learning,\nfetch occupancy or any checker to obtain the timing result.\n\nRetain all existing tests. Add focused registered-match transitions\nfor both sources, younger writers to the same rd, x0 and non-writers,\nqueued decode, WB collisions, load-use bubbles, dmem holds with\nvalid-cleared WB history, MUL/DIV producer drain and response-edge\nconsumers, redirects and reset. Check results and RVFI operands against\nindependent architectural expectations and verify each store and\nretirement once. Run the unchanged formal suite and full cosim gates,\nthen repeat canonical stalled CoreMark and all three Gowin placements.\nAt unchanged cycles acceptance needs median Fmax above 59.162 MHz and\nfitness above 145.729 iter/sec. Forecast a 27 percent fitness gain,\nwith medium confidence pending formal. Remaining predictor eligibility,\ndivider recurrence and added flop routing can limit final timing;\nre-measure cycles and median Fmax rather than assuming the prototype.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
