diction_direct_match, then the existing source fields. Retain\n  the original saved predicted_next_pc for dynamic JALR verification.\n\n  In EX use the registered sequential candidate for jump link data,\n  architectural sequential pc_next, saved MUL/DIV sequential metadata\n  and se\n…[3951 of 7023 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0198bd99374a930c]…\nn parallel before ID/EX. Capture and hold\n      them with existing payload rules, independently of flush.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Consume registered candidates and match bits for sequential and\n      direct target resolution, jump links, traps, training, recovery\n      and architectural/saved next PCs. Keep dynamic JALR arithmetic,\n      exact comparison, actual outcome selection and all handshakes.\n  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Adapt packed bundle drivers and retain all result, trap, bypass,\n      M arithmetic/latency/response-hold checks. Extend independently\n      calculated candidate/match cases and stale-prediction recovery.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Adapt internal ID/EX field monitors while preserving all ISA/RVFI\n      expectations. Verify full-width candidate arithmetic, exact match\n      selection, held metadata and immediate recovery across queue\n      states, load/M dependencies, faults and independent bus stalls.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
