{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'structural|hyp-20260930-002-r2s1|hyp-20260930-001-r2s0' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260930-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Move division out of the combinational execute path\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The only recorded bench experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12,\\nmedian Fmax 5.442 MHz, and a 199.837 ns path through forwarding and\\nu_ex/u_alu with 156 cells. No LESSONS.md or earlier structural attempts\\nexist in this fixture. The ALU implements signed and unsigned division\\nand remainder with combinational / and % operators. These are likely\\nresponsible for the very deep arithmetic path; even instructions that\\ndo not divide must meet the clock constraint imposed by that hardware.\\nMoving this arithmetic behind registers should substantially improve\\nFmax, at the cost of additional cycles only for DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only recorded bench experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12,\\nmedian Fmax 5.442 MHz, and a 199.837 ns path through forwarding and\\nu_ex/u_alu with 156 cells. No LESSONS.md or earlier structural attempts\\nexist in this fixture. The ALU implements signed and unsigned division\\nand remainder with combinational / and % operators. These are likely\\nresponsible for the very deep arithmetic path; even instructions that\\ndo not divide must meet the clock constraint imposed by that hardware.\\nMoving this arithmetic behind registers should substantially improve\\nFmax, at the cost of additional cycles only for DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational divide/remainder cone with one shared,\\nblocking, registered divider in EX. Use unsigned restoring division\\nwith four explicitly bounded quotient-bit steps per clock, eight\\niteration clocks, operand magnitude capture at launch, and signed\\ncorrection on completion. Target at most ten EX clocks from accepting\\na request to transferring its result under zero-wait memory, and at\\nmost ten clocks between successive retirements for back-to-back divide\\ninstructions. This keeps progress inside the existing formal liveness\\nwindow without changing any checker. Each\n…[28987 of 32059 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b9b7decffb870049]…\nment\", \"fitness\": 103.38, \"delta_pct\": 20.29, \"vs_baseline\": 752.97, \"fmax_mhz\": 46.433, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3105, \"ff\": 678, \"seeds\": [44.784, 46.433, 46.433], \"perturbations\": [[0, 44.784, 23], [1, 46.433, 25], [2, 46.433, 25]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_3_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs2_val_0_s100\", \"slack_ns\": -17.329, \"arrival_ns\": 27.624, \"logic_cells\": 43, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_hazard\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 23, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-30T14:14:29.994927Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 2, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-002-r2s1 (improvement, +20.29%): Two radix-4 digits per iteration with parallel D/2D/3D subtraction and a response register before sign correction shorten the divider-to-EX/MEM path, while a four-bit launch seed preserves nine-clock EX latency.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
