{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_35", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"git status --short; sed -n '1,200p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-002-r3s1.yaml\"", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20260930-002-r3s1\ntitle: \"Separate redirect squash from instruction payload capture\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 103.38 at median Gowin Fmax 46.433 MHz, with\n  4,491,485 measured CoreMark cycles. Its reported worst path starts\n  at EX/MEM destination state and crosses forwarding, execute, fetch,\n  hazards, and decode before reaching an ID/EX operand register:\n  27.624 ns through 43 cells. The earlier radix-4 timing probe also\n  exposed this register-read/branch-flush/decode cone. Both prior\n  structural hypotheses addressed division successfully; the critical\n  path has now moved to control feeding back into the front-end data.\n  Fetch currently replaces the entire instruction with a NOP on a\n  redirect, and ID flush zeroes its entire payload. Thus late branch\n  resolution selects register addresses, decode results and operand\n  data in the same clock. A register-boundary restructuring can remove\n  that feedback without adding a branch bubble or changing division.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split the front end's instruction payload path from its validity and\n  squash path. Preserve the existing pipeline depth, EX branch resolve,\n  single retirement, bus handshakes and instruction cycle schedule.\n  A redirect must change the PC and invalidate the younger ID/EX entry,\n  but must have no combinational influence on that entry's instruction\n  bits, register-file read addresses, decoded controls, immediate,\n  operand payload D inputs or payload capture enable.\n\n  In IF, continuously present the unmodified imem_data and current PC\n  to decode. Remove the redirect/flush-controlled NOP substitution.\n  Fetch validity still rejects unavailable instruction data and the\n  wrong-path instruction on a redirect. Preserve reset PC and the\n  rule that redirect overrides instruction-bus stalls. Invalid fetch\n  payloads may contain arbitrary decoded operations; validity alone\n  determines whether they enter the architectural pipeline.\n\n  In ID, implement independent sequential updates for payload and\n  vali\n…[3525 of 6597 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:01aeb09ee4015739]…\nhazard. Keep redirect\n      solely in squash and PC control, outside payload hold logic.\n      Preserve dmem/division holds, bubble timing and WB retention.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire any raw-fetch availability qualifier required by hazard\n      detection independently of redirect-masked validity. Audit valid\n      gating of all downstream side effects without changing top-level\n      IO, retirement width, forwarding priorities or divider timing.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Retain existing tests and add forwarded branch and JAL/JALR squash\n      cases with imem/dmem stalls, a held older load/store, and wrong-path\n      stores, illegal instructions and divisions. Verify exact RVFI\n      source values and PC order, no wrong-path memory/divider service,\n      no duplicate side effects, contiguous retirement order, and the\n      existing division progress bounds. Check that invalid payloads\n      with nonzero side-effect controls remain architecturally inert.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nfrom tools.eval.fpga import validate_coremark_uart\np=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/5ff8876e/b084c97c/structural_squash_probe/coremark_output.jsonl')\nlines=p.read_text().splitlines()\nmarker=json.loads(lines[-1])\nassert marker['ebreak'] and not marker['oob'] and marker['bench_bracketed']\nvalid, reason=validate_coremark_uart(marker['uart'], 10)\nassert valid, reason\ncycles=marker['bench_stop_cycle']-marker['bench_start_cycle']\nassert cycles > 0\nresult={'completed':True, 'cycles':cycles, 'canonical_crcs_passed':valid, 'marker_bracketed':True, 'oob':marker['oob'], 'fitness_probe':50.089e6*10/cycles, 'delta_pct':(50.089e6*10/cycles/103.38-1)*100}\np.with_name('coremark_result.json').write_text(json.dumps(result, indent=2))\nprint(json.dumps(result, indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
