{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nrows=[json.loads(s) for s in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]\nfor r in rows:\n if r.get('category')=='structural':\n  print(json.dumps({k:r.get(k) for k in ('id','title','fitness','fmax_mhz','cycles','critical_path')},indent=2))\n  h=r.get('hypothesis',{})\n  if isinstance(h,dict): print(h.get('hypothesis',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260930-002-r1s1\",\n  \"title\": \"Move division out of the combinational execute path\",\n  \"fitness\": 85.94,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 38.602,\n  \"cycles\": 4491485,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider/remainder_q_5_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -20.969,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 31.264,\n    \"logic_cells\": 136,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\nReplace the combinational divide/remainder cone with one shared,\nblocking, registered divider in EX. Use unsigned restoring division\nwith four explicitly bounded quotient-bit steps per clock, eight\niteration clocks, operand magnitude capture at launch, and signed\ncorrection on completion. Target at most ten EX clocks from accepting\na request to transferring its result under zero-wait memory, and at\nmost ten clocks between successive retirements for back-to-back divide\ninstructions. This keeps progress inside the existing formal liveness\nwindow without changing any checker. Each iteration uses a 33-bit\npartial remainder and subtract/borrow selection; do not infer / or %\nor unroll all 32 quotient steps into a single combinational path.\nPreserve single-cycle execution of every other ALU operation, including\nthe existing multipliers, to make this one divider-focused structural\nchange. A four-step iteration is a timing/latency