{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom tools.eval.gowin import build_all,parse_reports, summarize\nwt=Path.cwd()\nprobe=wt/'cores/bench/generated/hypgen_probe2'\nr=build_all(wt,probe/'rtl','fpga/core_bench_si.sv',probe/'timing',options=(1,2))\np0=parse_reports(probe/'timing/gowin_p0'); p0['place_option']=0\nr=[p0]+r\nprint(r)\nprint('SCORE',summarize(r))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_27", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml, json, jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-002-r6s1.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Explicit flop register file preserves the operand pipeline boundary'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 132.98 iter/sec at 53.987 MHz and 4,059,766\nbracketed CoreMark cycles. Its worst Gowin path starts in the inferred\nregister-file memory and reaches divider initialization through ID\nand EX: 24.55 ns through 22 cells. Divider-only retiming exposed a\nsecond register-file-to-branch path and lost fitness. The common source\nis operand delivery. Making the ID/EX operand registers real flip-flop\nboundaries can shorten several arithmetic and branch paths together.\n'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Replace the architectural integer register file's large inferred\nmemory with 31 explicit 32-bit flip-flop register words and two complete\ncombinational read-selection networks. Use separately declared words\nor a generate structure of individual scalar words with dedicated\nwrite-address qualification, rather than a variable-indexed memory\narray that Gowin can infer as BSRAM. Keep x0 a literal zero. Preserve\nreset-to-zero for every architectural word, the single synchronous\nwrite port, and same-cycle write-first bypass on both read ports.\n\nComplete ALL source selection, including zero qualification and\nsame-cycle WB bypass, before the existing ID/EX operand registers.\nPreserve those two 32-bit operand registers as the timing boundary;\ndo not move a bank-selection or delayed-WB mux into EX. EX receives\nregistered base operands and retains its existing EX/MEM-over-MEM/WB\nover-base forwarding priority. There is no added instruction stage,\nregistered-address delay, bank mux after ID/EX, or change to instruction\nissue/retirement schedules. This is a single structural replacement of\nthe register-file storage implementation and its synthesis boundary,\nnot a rename or a circuit-neutral placement perturbation.\n\nUse portable resettable flop RTL with a full 32-address case read or\nan equivalent complete decode and balanced selection network. Reject\nwrites to x0 and suppress reset-time writes exactly as the current\nmodule does. Keep the existing register-file interface, ID payload\nholds, validity-only flush, retained MEM/WB forwarding history, and\nlaunch-once saved sources for multiplication/division unchanged.\nReset, stalls, and redirects must retain the same architectural\nbehavior. No arithmetic operation, predictor policy, fetch queue,\nload-use bubble, decoder legality rule, bus handshake, nret=1 port,\nRVFI source field, retirement order, or progress bound changes.\n\nAn isolated proposal-stage prototype changed only reg_file.sv into\nexplicit words with complete case-based reads before ID/EX. All 39\nunchanged pipeline tests passed. Gowin placement option 0 measured\n56.335 MHz using 4,937 LUT4s, 1,964 FFs, 24 LUT-RAMs, 7 BSRAMs and two\nDSPs. The worst path moved from register-file memory to WB forwarding\nselection, reaching divider launch/address arithmetic at 23.045 ns.\nThis establishes that the structural boundary is effective; it is\nnot yet a median-Fmax or full implementation-phase acceptance result.\n\nRetain all register-file tests, including reset after arbitrary writes,\nboth read ports, same-cycle write-first bypass and x0. Add bank-spanning\narchitectural dependencies and younger-forwarding-priority checks if\nneeded. Run the unchanged formal gates and canonical stalled CoreMark\nwith access bounds, validation literal, exact CRCs and MMIO timing\nbrackets. Inspect synthesis to require 31 architectural flop words and\nactual ID/EX operand registers, rather than a BSRAM read extending into\nEX. Judge median vendor Fmax times measured iterations/cycle. With\nunchanged bracketed cycles the 4.6 percent acceptance threshold is\n56.47 MHz. Area and routing increase, and forwarding/divider paths may\ncap the gain; no checker or clock count may be relaxed to compensate.\n'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'}\nd['changes']=[\n {'file':'rtl/reg_file.sv','description':'''Replace the variable-indexed register memory with 31 explicit resettable\n32-bit flop words and complete combinational reads. Keep the existing\ninterface, x0, single synchronous write, deterministic reset and both\nwrite-first bypasses. Preserve the existing ID/EX operand register\nboundary; no post-boundary bank-selection mux is introduced.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_reg_file.py','description':'''Preserve every current architectural register-file check. Extend\ncoverage to all source/destination addresses, both simultaneous WB\ncollisions, reset after populated state, and ignored x0 writes without\nchanging the combinational-read or synchronous-write interface.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain all existing forwarding, stall, queue, arithmetic and RVFI\nchecks. Add dependencies across the full register address range and\nsame-edge WB read collisions as needed; preserve source correctness,\nheld forwarding history and ten-clock ready-bus division bounds.\n'''}]\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Refined hypothesis validates')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
