{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"category\\\":\\\\s*\\\"structural\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20260930-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Move division out of the combinational execute path\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The only recorded bench experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12,\\nmedian Fmax 5.442 MHz, and a 199.837 ns path through forwarding and\\nu_ex/u_alu with 156 cells. No LESSONS.md or earlier structural attempts\\nexist in this fixture. The ALU implements signed and unsigned division\\nand remainder with combinational / and % operators. These are likely\\nresponsible for the very deep arithmetic path; even instructions that\\ndo not divide must meet the clock constraint imposed by that hardware.\\nMoving this arithmetic behind registers should substantially improve\\nFmax, at the cost of additional cycles only for DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only recorded bench experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12,\\nmedian Fmax 5.442 MHz, and a 199.837 ns path through forwarding and\\nu_ex/u_alu with 156 cells. No LESSONS.md or earlier structural attempts\\nexist in this fixture. The ALU implements signed and unsigned division\\nand remainder with combinational / and % operators. These are likely\\nresponsible for the very deep arithmetic path; even instructions that\\ndo not divide must meet the clock constraint imposed by that hardware.\\nMoving this arithmetic behind registers should substantially improve\\nFmax, at the cost of additional cycles only for DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational divide/remainder cone with one shared,\\nblocking, registered divider in EX. Use unsigned restoring division\\nwith four explicitly bounded quotient-bit steps per clock, eight\\niteration clocks, operand magnitude capture at launch, and signed\\ncorrection on completion. Target at most ten EX clocks from accepting\\na request to transferring its result under zero-wait memory, and at\\nmost ten clocks between successive retirements for back-to-back divide\\ninstructions. This keeps progress inside the existing formal liveness\\nwindow without changing any checker. Each i\n…[61457 of 64529 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4ee21956641ab70a]…\nmhz\": 56.223, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4059766, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4937, \"ff\": 1964, \"seeds\": [56.335, 56.223, 56.223], \"perturbations\": [[0, 56.335, 21], [1, 56.223, 21], [2, 56.223, 21]], \"lutram\": 24, \"bsram\": 7, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_1_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider/remainder_q_2_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -12.751, \"arrival_ns\": 23.045, \"logic_cells\": 24, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 21, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-30T17:22:29.390696Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 6, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-002-r6s1 (regression, +4.14%): Explicit resettable register-file words and complete case reads before ID/EX remove the inferred-memory operand path, but the prototype exposes WB forwarding into divider launch/address arithmetic as the next timing bottleneck, leaving the final gain below the 4.6% acceptance threshold.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
