t\nabove 139.32. The worst option-0 path moved to producer eligibility\nand predictor update, with 19.969 ns arrival, instead of the original\nregister-tag or RF-memory operand path. These are proposal-stage\nmeasurements; unchanged formal and full implementation-phase gates\nremain mandatory before acceptance.\n\nPreserve nret=1 and the exact core IO, sole channel-0 retirement,\nstrict order +1, decoder default-illegal discipline, EBREAK-only SYSTEM\nlegality, alignment traps, memory-request stability, one-time side\neffects, validity-only decode recovery, reset cancellation, exact\nnine-edge DIV and three-edge MUL transactions, ALTOPS formulas and\nreal RV32M arithmetic. Keep every existing ten-clock ready-bus division\nretirement check. Do not change arithmetic, predictor learning,\nfetch occupancy or any checker to obtain the timing result.\n\nRetain all existing tests. Add focused registered-match transitions\nfor both sources, younger writers to the same rd, x0 and non-writers,\nqueued decode, WB collisions, load-use bubbles, dmem holds with\nvalid-cleared WB history, MUL/DIV producer drain and response-edge\nconsumers, redirects and reset. Check results and RVFI operands against\nindependent architectural expectations and verify each store and\nretirement once. Run the unchanged formal suite and full cosim gates,\nthen repeat canonical stalled CoreMark and all three Gowin placements.\nAt unchanged cycles acceptance needs median Fmax above 59.162 MHz and\nfitness above 145.729 iter/sec. Forecast a 27 percent fitness gain,\nwith medium confidence pending formal. Remaining predictor eligibility,\ndivider recurrence and added flop routing can limit final timing;\nre-measure cycles and median Fmax rather than assuming the prototype.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':27,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/reg_file.sv','description':'''Replace inferred storage with 31 explicit scalar resettable flop\nwords and complete case reads. Keep x0, synchronous writes, both WB\nwrite-first bypasses and the existing interface. Complete all source\nselection before ID/EX, preserving architectural reset semantics.\n'''},\n {'file':'rtl/forward_unit.sv','description':'''Replace live EX register-tag comparisons with four match registers\ncomputed for accepted queue-head sources against destinations moving\nto EX/MEM and MEM/WB. Freeze on dmem hold; shift EX matches to WB and\nclear EX matches when older stages drain during a decode hold. Keep\nactual write qualification, younger priority and retained WB history.\n'''},\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Wire clock/reset, stall_id, stall_ex_mem, queue-head source addresses,\ncurrent ID/EX and EX/MEM destinations, and actual producer write\neligibility to the retimed forwarding unit. Keep EX forwarding-select\noutputs and all external IO, pipeline movement and nret=1 retirement.\n'''},\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'''Add a 32-bit preselected wb_data field to mem_wb_t, preserving all\nexisting pipeline and RVFI fields and compilation-unit compatibility.\n'''},\n {'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'''Register the load-versus-ALU result selection into MEM/WB.wb_data\non normal capture. Reset it and retain it under dmem hold along with\nthe existing payload while clearing only valid. Keep load extraction,\nalignment traps, byte lanes, side effects and RVFI metadata unchanged.\n'''},\n {'file':'rtl/wb_stage.sv','description':'''Drive w_data directly from MEM/WB.wb_data instead of selecting between\nread_data and alu_result after the register. Preserve current write\nenable and destination behavior; RF and EX bypass use this same value.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_reg_file.py','description':'''Retain all current reset, both-read-port, write-first and x0 tests.\nExtend address-spanning reads/writes and simultaneous WB collisions\nwithout changing expected combinational-read/synchronous-write timing.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_forward_unit.py','description':'''Add an isolated clocked forwarding-control suite for capture, both\nsource matches, younger priority, non-writers, x0, producer migration,\ndmem hold, retained WB eligibility, response-edge capture and reset.\nUse an independent producer/consumer sequence model for selection.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Preserve every current architectural, queue, predictor, arithmetic,\nlatency and RVFI assertion. Extend repeated-writer/both-source hazards,\nqueued sources, WB collisions, valid-cleared forwarding history and\nMUL/DIV drain/response consumers; verify exact operands, side effects,\nretirement order and unchanged ten-clock ready-bus division bounds.\n'''}\n]}\nclass ReadableDumper(yaml.SafeDumper):\n pass\ndef represent_str(dumper,value):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',value,style='|' if '\\\\n' in value else None)\nReadableDumper.add_representer(str,represent_str)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(h,Dumper=ReadableDumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\nparsed=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\njsonschema.validate(parsed,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nassert parsed['id']=='hyp-20260930-002-r7s1'\nassert parsed['category']=='structural'\nassert type(parsed['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nassert -50 <= parsed['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct'] <= 50\nassert all(c['file'].startswith(('rtl/','test/test_')) for c in parsed['changes'])\nprint('Wrote and schema-validated',p)\nprint('Prototype projected fitness:',72.124e6 * 10/4059766)\nprint('Gain over rounded champion:',(72.124e6 * 10/4059766 /139.32 - 1)*100)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Wrote and schema-validated cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-002-r7s1.yaml\nPrototype projected fitness: 177.65555945835303\nGain over rounded champion: 27.516192548344122\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
