stall payload update rule as PC, instruction, immediate, and prediction.\nPreserve validity-only flushes, with flush taking priority over holds\nfor valid alone. Do not gate the raw instruction, decoder, register-file\naddresses, or payload enables with redirect. Bubbles may retain decoded\nfields; existing stage-valid qualification must continue to isolate them.\n\nIn EX, replace in.pc + 4 with the registered sequential candidate and\nreplace in.pc + in.imm with the registered direct candidate for branch\nand JAL target resolution, target alignment checks, predictor training,\ncorrective redirect targets, architectural pc_next, and jump link data.\nReplace the current sequential_match and direct_match comparators with\ntheir register\n…[4123 of 7195 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:3ef258441a35a081]…\n (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
