{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_50", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r11s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20260930-003-r11s2\ntitle: \"Register exact prediction checks before branch resolution\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion reaches 191.13 iter/sec at 77.593 MHz, but its worst path\n  starts at an ID/EX operand and crosses EX, IF, EX and decode. Predictor\n  training retiming regressed repeatedly, and the resolved return stack\n  saved only 2,196 of 4,059,766 CoreMark cycles. Shortening immediate\n  prediction verification is more promising than adding predictor state.\n  The earlier r4s2 candidate moved operand-independent recovery work into\n  ID and gained 6.29 percent against its then-parent, although another\n  slot won that round; the current operand boundary makes a focused\n  retest worthwhile.\nhypothesis: |\n  Move exact sequential/direct prediction verification into the existing\n  ID/EX boundary. Preserve the 64-entry fully tagged next-PC table, its\n  two-bit counters and immediate EX training, the two-entry fall-through\n  queue, immediate corrective redirect, pipeline depth and nret=1 ports.\n  This is one prediction-verification timing change.\n\n  From each IF/ID bundle, calculate actual sequential_candidate = PC+4\n  and direct_candidate = PC+decoded_immediate with full 32-bit arithmetic.\n  Compare the instruction's exact saved predicted_next_pc against both\n  candidates. Capture both resolved candidates and their one-bit equality\n  results with the existing ID/EX payload under the existing !stall enable.\n  Retain predicted_next_pc for dynamic JALR verification. Queued fetches\n  must use their saved PC and prediction rather than the current bus PC\n  or a refreshed table lookup. Flush still changes only stage validity.\n\n  In EX use the registered sequential candidate for ordinary/illegal\n  next PC and JAL/JALR link values; use the registered direct candidate\n  for conditional-branch and JAL targets, alignment checks and training.\n  Select the registered equality bit after the actual branch outcome\n  and existing legality/fault checks. Keep rs1+immediate, bit-zero\n  clearing, alignment and exac\n…[1682 of 4754 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f836afad69370990]…\nile retaining saved predicted_next_pc.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Compute candidates and full-width prediction equalities from the\n      presented IF/ID bundle, then capture them with the existing payload\n      enable; retain validity-only flushes and all operand delivery.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Use the registered candidates and match bits for sequential/direct\n      resolution, link values, alignment and training. Retain dynamic\n      JALR computation and immediate once-per-advance exact correction.\n  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Adapt packed ID/EX stimulus and independently check selected match\n      equivalence, resolved targets, link values and existing M holds.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Cover full-width PC carry/wrap, offsets, target equal to fall-through,\n      stale predictions, faults, queues and independent bus/M holds with\n      exact RVFI PCs, order and absence of wrong-path memory effects.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
