{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_83", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r12s2.yaml')\np.write_text('''id: hyp-20260930-003-r12s2\ntitle: \\\"Parallel carry-consistency verification of predicted next PCs\\\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 200.89 iter/sec at 81.557 MHz and 4,059,766\n  bracketed CoreMark cycles. The earlier return stack saved only 2,196\n  cycles, and both recent table-banking attempts lost Fmax. Accuracy\n  and capacity therefore have little demonstrated headroom. Current\n  recovery compares a saved prediction with three newly added PCs:\n  PC+4, PC+imm and rs1+imm with bit zero cleared. This serializes a\n  carry-propagating addition and a wide equality on the predictor\n  verification path. Early equality-register probes moved the critical\n  path into IF/ID and regressed; verify the addition relation directly\n  in EX instead, with parallel local carry constraints.\nhypothesis: |\n  Change only the combinational verification of the existing predictor's\n  exact saved next PC. Keep its 64-entry fully tagged table, complete\n  thirty-bit aligned targets, two-bit counters, immediate training,\n  two-entry fall-through queue, accepted predictions, recovery latency\n  and instruction schedule unchanged. Replace the EX sequential_match,\n  direct_match and jalr_match adder-then-equality expressions with an\n  exact parallel carry-consistency equality circuit. Leave independent\n  architectural target arithmetic and all ALU arithmetic unchanged.\n\n  For 32-bit operands A and B and prediction P, define the required\n  carry into each bit as C = P xor A xor B. Define the locally generated\n  carry vector G = (A and B) or ((A xor B) and C). P equals the low\n  thirty-two bits of A+B iff C[0] is zero and C[31:1] equals G[30:0].\n  Every local condition is computed concurrently: do not ripple C,\n  instantiate an adder, or infer a subtraction for this verification.\n  Combine the thirty-two agreement bits with a balanced 32-to-16-to-8-\n  to-4-to-2-to-1 AND tree. Discard only carry out of bit 31, as required\n  by RV32 modulo arithmetic; no PC, target or comparison bit is truncated.\n\n  Use A=instruction PC and B=4 for sequential_match; use A=PC and\n  B=the decoded immediate for direct_match. For JALR, use A=the final\n  registered/standalone-forwarded rs1 and B=the decoded immediate.\n  JALR clears the SUM's bit zero, while its original addition still\n  generates a carry into bit one. Set required C[0] to zero, independently\n  require P[0]=0, and retain every higher carry constraint. G[0] is then\n  A[0] and B[0], preserving the true carry into bit one. Do not clear\n  either operand's low bit, and do not discard the low-bit carry.\n  This variant is exactly P == ((A+B) & 0xfffffffe), including wraparound.\n\n  Preserve the existing outcome/legality/alignment selection of the\n  three match bits and redirect = qualified EX advance and mismatch.\n  Keep the independently computed real sequential PC, branch/JAL\n  target and JALR sum for resolved_next_pc, corrective target, jump\n  link values, target alignment checks, predictor training and RVFI.\n  A prediction must never replace architectural arithmetic. Preserve\n  equality even when direct and sequential targets coincide, when\n  predictions differ only in high bits, and when stale table entries\n  now fetch ordinary, illegal, misaligned or blocking M instructions.\n\n  This is one predictor-verification timing change, with no new pipeline\n  field, table organization, prediction policy or recovery bubble.\n  Preserve once-per-advance training, old-data lookup, immutable queued\n  predictions, validity-only younger squash, redirect priority, bus\n  backpressure, load-use bubbling, complete decode operand bypass,\n  MUL/DIV capture/hold/response behavior and real/ALTOPS arithmetic.\n  Preserve nret=1 ports, architectural RVFI values, contiguous order,\n  forward progress, decoder legality and every memory/CRC/UART/marker\n  invariant. No evaluation file, formal bound or checker may change.\n\n  Test the three match outputs against an independent integer-addition\n  oracle. Cover exhaustive small-width carry patterns embedded at every\n  bit position, zero/all-ones, alternating bit patterns, long carry runs,\n  signed-looking immediates, high-bit-only mismatches, PC wraparound,\n  direct/sequential coincidence and deterministic random full-width\n  triples. Exercise both matching and deliberately corrupted predictions.\n  For JALR cover all operand low-bit combinations, carry from bit zero,\n  both predicted low-bit values, wraparound and standalone forwarding.\n  Retain every existing branch/ALU/M transaction and pipeline assertion.\n  Run unchanged nret=1 formal including liveness, reference cosim,\n  and canonical stalled CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/start-stop validation.\n\n  Forecast six percent fitness improvement at unchanged CoreMark cycles\n  by shortening exact prediction verification without moving the cone\n  across IF/ID. Confidence is low until all three Gowin placement options\n  finish. At 4,059,766 cycles acceptance requires median Fmax above\n  approximately 85.309 MHz and fitness above 210.131 iter/sec. The\n  independently resolved target adder and unchanged divider can become\n  limiting, and vendor mapping may favor native carry chains; report\n  measured median Fmax and bracketed cycles rather than counting LUTs.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Implement exact parallel carry-consistency equality with a balanced\n      agreement reduction for sequential, direct and bit-zero-cleared\n      JALR predictions. Preserve all architectural adders, match selection,\n      recovery/training qualification, payloads and arithmetic handshakes.\n  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Add independent full-width arithmetic-oracle checks of all three\n      verification outputs over carry patterns, wraparound, corrupted\n      predictions, JALR low-bit carry and forwarding. Retain every existing\n      branch, trap, bypass, saved-response, hold and reset assertion.\n''')\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nv=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\njsonschema.validate(v,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Updated predictor hypothesis validates:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
