{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'predictor|next-PC|return|branch|BTB|gshare|bimodal|RAS' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260930-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Move division out of the combinational execute path\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The only recorded bench experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12,\\nmedian Fmax 5.442 MHz, and a 199.837 ns path through forwarding and\\nu_ex/u_alu with 156 cells. No LESSONS.md or earlier structural attempts\\nexist in this fixture. The ALU implements signed and unsigned division\\nand remainder with combinational / and % operators. These are likely\\nresponsible for the very deep arithmetic path; even instructions that\\ndo not divide must meet the clock constraint imposed by that hardware.\\nMoving this arithmetic behind registers should substantially improve\\nFmax, at the cost of additional cycles only for DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only recorded bench experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12,\\nmedian Fmax 5.442 MHz, and a 199.837 ns path through forwarding and\\nu_ex/u_alu with 156 cells. No LESSONS.md or earlier structural attempts\\nexist in this fixture. The ALU implements signed and unsigned division\\nand remainder with combinational / and % operators. These are likely\\nresponsible for the very deep arithmetic path; even instructions that\\ndo not divide must meet the clock constraint imposed by that hardware.\\nMoving this arithmetic behind registers should substantially improve\\nFmax, at the cost of additional cycles only for DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational divide/remainder cone with one shared,\\nblocking, registered divider in EX. Use unsigned restoring division\\nwith four explicitly bounded quotient-bit steps per clock, eight\\niteration clocks, operand magnitude capture at launch, and signed\\ncorrection on completion. Target at most ten EX clocks from accepting\\na request to transferring its result under zero-wait memory, and at\\nmost ten clocks between successive retirements for back-to-back divide\\ninstructions. This keeps progress inside the existing formal liveness\\nwindow without changing any checker. Each\n…[86950 of 90022 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:01645c2bb7f1a7c3]…\ns\": 117.75, \"delta_pct\": 13.9, \"vs_baseline\": 871.53, \"fmax_mhz\": 49.426, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4197517, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3662, \"ff\": 902, \"seeds\": [46.008, 49.426, 49.426], \"perturbations\": [[0, 46.008, 15], [1, 49.426, 15], [2, 49.426, 15]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 9, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -16.735, \"arrival_ns\": 27.03, \"logic_cells\": 15, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 15, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-30T14:58:26.933219Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 3, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-003-r3s2 (improvement, +13.90%): Pairing 64-entry tagged next-PC prediction with the retimed divider and validity-only ID/EX recovery converts CoreMark's taken-transfer bubble savings into a throughput gain by keeping redirect out of instruction decode and payload capture enables.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
