{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_50", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r5s2.yaml')\nx={\n'id':'hyp-20260930-003-r5s2',\n'title':'Two-entry predicted-path lookahead hides instruction stalls',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion already has a 64-entry next-PC predictor, but its fetch PC\nis frozen whenever decode is held by load-use, data-memory backpressure,\nor blocking MUL/DIV. Thus it cannot fetch predicted-path instructions\nduring those otherwise unused bus opportunities. About 22 percent of\ninstruction-bus cycles stall independently of those holds. A tiny elastic\nqueue can retain useful predicted-path fetches during holds and supply\nthem when the pipeline resumes despite a coincident instruction stall.\nThis targets iterations per cycle rather than marginal branch accuracy.\nPrior predictor accuracy improvements have little remaining headroom;\nisolated early-verification prototypes on this champion reduced Fmax.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Decouple the existing next-PC predictor's fetch traversal from decode\nacceptance with one two-entry fall-through predicted-instruction queue\ninside IF. Preserve the current 64-entry tagged target/direction predictor,\nits policy, all arithmetic, stage depth, and nret=1 retirement. Each queued\nentry holds the fetched PC, raw 32-bit instruction, and the exact 32-bit\npredicted_next_pc selected when that fetch was accepted. This is a single\npredicted-path lookahead mechanism; do not add a cache, another predictor,\nnew arithmetic units, or a deeper execute pipeline.\n\nOn each ready instruction-bus cycle, accept the current fetch when the\nqueue has space or an existing head is simultaneously consumed. Advance\nthe fetch PC to that fetch's prediction independently of load-use, dmem,\nmultiplier, and divider holds. Stop only when the queue is full, the bus\nis unavailable, reset is active, or EX is correcting the path. When empty,\nlet the current ready fetch fall directly through into decode, retaining\nthe champion's zero-extra-stage common case. A consumed fall-through\ninstruction advances the fetch PC without occupying the queue. When a\nqueued head exists, present its PC/instruction/saved prediction to ID and\nconsume it exactly once when ID/EX can capture a valid instruction without\na flush. Support simultaneous enqueue/dequeue, including full occupancy,\nwith old-data head semantics. Never enqueue an unavailable bus response.\n\nSeparate raw imem readiness from instruction availability to decode.\nAvailability is queue_nonempty OR raw_imem_ready, independently of\nredirect masking. Drive hazard load-use operand comparisons from the\nactual head/fall-through instruction, rather than raw io_imemData from\nthe speculative fetch PC. Use this availability for load-use qualification\nand for inserting an instruction-unavailable bubble; a raw bus stall must\nnot suppress an already queued instruction. Pass the decode hold to the\nqueue's consumption logic; the old global stall_if no longer controls the\nspeculative fetch PC. Preserve dmem freeze, arithmetic holds, retained\nMEM/WB forwarding, and the one-cycle load-use bubble.\n\nPreserve validity-only ID/EX correction and keep redirect out of raw\ninstruction decode, register-file addresses, and payload clock enables.\nOn a valid advancing EX mismatch, discard every queued younger entry,\nsuppress enqueue/dequeue on that edge, and set the fetch PC to the actual\nresolved target with priority over a full queue or bus/decode hold. EX\ncontinues comparing every instruction's saved full-width prediction with\nits architectural next PC, including stale hits on ordinary, illegal,\nmisaligned, MUL, and DIV instructions. Queued predictions must never be\nrecomputed from a table that may have changed since enqueue. Keep existing\nonce-per-EX-advance training; do not train prefetched or squashed entries.\nQueued instructions create no memory or register side effects until they\nadvance through the existing validated pipeline.\n\nReset queue occupancy and pointers, leaving payload storage unreset and\nunobservable while empty. Keep queue payload capture independent of EX\nredirect by qualifying write events and clearing occupancy on correction;\nnever mux redirect into instruction or decoder data. Preserve full PC\nwidth, correct old-data behavior at simultaneous table training, decoder\nlegality, trap rules, exact RVFI PCs/order, and the top-level IO contract.\n\nExtend pipeline tests for empty fall-through, filling while ID is held,\nfull-queue backpressure, simultaneous full enqueue/dequeue, head delivery\nwhile raw imemReady is low, and corrections at every occupancy. Exercise\nload-to-branch hazards using a head different from raw fetch data, older\nblocked loads/stores, MUL/DIV drain and response edges, stale entries,\nchanging JALR targets, illegal/misaligned transfers, reset, and wrong-path\nstores in both queue slots. Check exact retirement sequences and bounded\nprogress, then run unchanged formal gates and canonical stalled CoreMark\nwith CRC/UART, bounds, and timing-marker checks. Evaluate median Gowin\nFmax times measured bracketed iterations per cycle. Forecast an 8 percent\nfitness gain from hiding instruction stalls, with low confidence until\nmeasured. Queue mux/clock-enable routing and additional wrong-path fetches\nare the main timing and throughput risks; correctness checks stay intact.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'''Add a two-entry fall-through queue carrying PC, raw instruction, and\nsaved next-PC prediction. Traverse the existing predictor whenever\nraw imem is ready and space is available, independent of decode holds.\nExpose decode availability, pop only accepted instructions, and clear\nall queued younger work on an advancing corrective redirect.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Wire raw imemReady and decode hold separately into IF. Feed hazard\nsource fields from the actual decoded queue head/fall-through bundle,\nand feed instruction availability to hazard fetch/bubble logic.\nPreserve all EX training, forwarding, and nret=1 external ports.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/hazard_unit.sv','description':'''Distinguish instruction availability to ID from raw bus readiness:\nqueued instructions remain consumable during imem stalls. Preserve\nraw-availability load-use qualification, decode/data-memory/arithmetic\nhold precedence, and validity-only corrective flushing.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Add directed queue occupancy, fall-through, simultaneous transfers,\nload-use head selection, held-pipeline prefetch, bus stall hiding,\nall-occupancy correction, wrong-path store suppression, arithmetic\nholds, reset, RVFI sequencing, and forward-progress checks.\n'''}]\n}\njsonschema.validate(x,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(x,sort_keys=False,width=85))\nprint('Revised hypothesis written and schema valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
