{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_28", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r6s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20260930-003-r6s2\ntitle: \"Region-qualified compact next-PC target prediction\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion already predicts with a fully tagged 64-entry next-PC table\n  and a two-entry fetch queue. Earlier doubling from 32 to 64 entries saved\n  only 11,157 cycles, and an architectural CoreMark trace suggests that a\n  return stack or a small history predictor would recover few additional\n  misses. The useful predictor opportunity is reducing target-table width\n  and routing cost while preserving the existing prediction behavior for\n  the compact CoreMark program. The predictor currently stores thirty target\n  bits for every entry even when the source and target occupy one 64 KiB\n  address region.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the thirty-bit target field in the existing 64-entry next-PC\n  predictor with fourteen target bits, guarded by a same-region installation\n  rule. Install a legal aligned control transfer only when the full resolved\n  target[31:16] equals its source PC[31:16]. Reconstruct a hit's complete\n  target as {fetch_pc[31:16], stored_target[15:2], 2'b00}. Keep the complete\n  existing PC tag, table index, conditional kind, two-bit direction counters,\n  queue, saved predicted_next_pc, and exact EX prediction verification.\n  This is lossless for transfers within a region and is a safe prediction\n  miss for every transfer crossing a region; architectural targets and RVFI\n  PCs remain full width. Do not globally truncate addresses or constrain the\n  supported ISA or program placement.\n\n  A legal cross-region transfer must not install a compressed target. If\n  its source matches an existing entry, invalidate that entry so a changing\n  JALR cannot retain an obsolete intra-region prediction. Nonmatching tags\n  remain untouched. Reset validity only and leave target storage unreset.\n  Maintain once-per-valid-EX-advance training, old-data lookup semantics,\n  validity-only correction, all bus/arithmetic hold behavior, and correction\n  priority over a full fetch queue. Compress only stored target bits: queued\n  and ID/EX predictions remain exact full-width PCs, and EX resolves and\n  compares all instructions independently of predictor state.\n\n  The objective is lower predictor memory width and fetch-PC routing pressure\n  at unchanged CoreMark cycles, allowing median Gowin Fmax to increase. Check\n  program control targets against the installation rule before reporting\n  unchanged cycles. Run the existing correctness gates and measure vendor\n  timing; routing improvements are uncertain and an IPC-only claim is not\n  sufficient. Add directed tests for both region boundaries, high addresses,\n  crossing and returning between regions, changing JALR targets, same-index\n  tags, saved queued predictions during invalidation, and stalled recovery.\n  Preserve nret=1, all decoder/trap rules, memory side effects, canonical\n  CoreMark CRCs, MMIO timing brackets, and every unchanged evaluation check.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Narrow the target array to target[15:2], reconstruct full-width targets\n      from the matching fetch PC region, qualify installations by equality\n      of source/target upper sixteen bits, and invalidate only matching\n      entries when a resolved transfer cannot be represented.\n  - file: test/test_if_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve queue and old-data tests while covering compact target lookup,\n      intra-region high PCs, cross-region miss/invalidation, full tags, region\n      boundaries, and queued full-width predictions retained across training.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Add full-width branch/JAL/JALR region-crossing retirement tests under\n      bus stalls and queued lookahead, checking architectural PCs, order,\n      link results, recovery, and absence of wrong-path stores.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
