{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='predictor':\n  print(json.dumps({k:d.get(k) for k in ['id','title','outcome','fitness','delta_pct','fmax_mhz','cycles','critical_path']}))\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  if isinstance(h,dict):\n   print(h.get('motivation',''))\n   if d['id'] in ['hyp-20260930-003-r4s2','hyp-20260930-003-r3s2']: print(h.get('hypothesis',''))\n  print(d.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20260930-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Small tagged next-PC predictor removes taken-control bubbles\", \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 12.81, \"delta_pct\": 5.69, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.393, \"cycles\": 4208674, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_3_dmem_3_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -190.81, \"arrival_ns\": 201.105, \"logic_cells\": 146, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}}\nThe baseline has no branch prediction: IF always selects PC+4, and EX\nredirects and squashes the combinational IF/ID instruction on every taken\nbranch, JAL, or JALR. Because IF/ID is not registered, this wastes one\nfetch opportunity per taken control transfer. CoreMark repeatedly executes\nloops and calls, so learning their direction and target should recover\nenough cycles to exceed the 4.6 percent acceptance threshold. The reported\nFmax bottleneck is the combinational arithmetic path; a small predictor\nshould improve iterations per cycle without lengthening that path. There\nare no recorded predictor attempts or distilled lessons in this fixture.\n\n\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260930-003-r2s2\", \"title\": \"64-entry next-PC prediction on the registered-divider champion\", \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 92.05, \"delta_pct\": 7.11, \"fmax_mhz\": 38.64, \"cycles\": 4197517, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider/divisor_q_1_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -23.192, \"arrival_ns\": 33.487, \"logic_cells\": 139, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}}\nThe current champion already removes combinational division from the\ntimed execute path and reaches 38.602 MHz at fitness 85.94, but still\nfetches PC+4 and discards one younger fetch on every taken control\ntransfer. The earlier predictor experiment hyp-20260930-003-r1s2\nreduced stalled CoreMark cycles from 4,491,485 to 4,208,674 (6.3%) and\npassed formal and cosim. Its fitness remained 12.81 because it was\nbuilt on the old combinational-divider baseline, not the champion.\nThis is evidence for a useful predictor rather\n…[17940 of 21012 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:bf625f8025ba6df9]…\n \"delta_pct\": -5.35, \"fmax_mhz\": 51.1, \"cycles\": 4059766, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider/remainder_q_0_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -14.851, \"arrival_ns\": 25.146, \"logic_cells\": 23, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider\"]}}\nThe champion already has a 64-entry fully tagged next-PC predictor and\ntwo-entry fetch lookahead. Earlier doubling from 32 to 64 entries saved\nonly 11,157 cycles, while a retired-stream profile of the canonical run\nsuggests little further benefit from a return stack or a small history\npredictor. A compact-target prototype also preserved 4,059,766 bracketed\ncycles but reduced median Gowin Fmax to 47.778 MHz. Its worst paths expose\nthe long forwarded-operand-to-predictor-update chain: EX branch/JALR\nresolution and alignment checks feed IF table write enables directly.\nDecoupling predictor learning from EX should reduce this fanout without\nadding latency to architectural branch recovery or changing arithmetic.\n\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
