{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_50", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport yaml, json, jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r7s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20260930-003-r7s2',\n'title':'Separate predictor payload allocation from target admissibility',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion already has a fully tagged 64-entry next-PC predictor and\ntwo-entry fetch queue. Earlier accuracy experiments show little remaining\ncycle headroom, and registering the complete training event reduced Fmax.\nCurrent vendor timing repeatedly crosses forwarding, EX, and IF table\nupdates: train_install includes target alignment derived from forwarded\nJALR operands and drives every tag, target, kind, and counter payload\nwrite enable. These payloads are harmless while their valid bit is clear,\nso their write enables need not wait for the late alignment decision.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Split predictor training into early payload allocation and late entry\nadmissibility, without delaying the training event or recovery. Preserve\nthe 64-entry fully tagged table, complete 30-bit aligned targets, current\ntwo-bit tagged direction policy, two-entry fall-through queue, arithmetic,\npipeline depth, and nret=1 ports. This is one predictor-update experiment.\n\nAdd an internal train_control signal from EX to IF, computed only from\nthe held decoded controls: \"'!in.ctrl.is_illegal AND (in.ctrl.is_branch OR\nin.ctrl.is_jump). Retain train_valid as the existing exactly-once valid\nEX-advance event qualified by reset, dmem freeze, and MUL/DIV completion.\nKeep train_install unchanged as the legal, aligned-target qualification.\n\nChange the tag/target/conditional/counter payload write enable to\n!reset AND train_valid AND train_control, rather than train_install.\nPreserve target data, full tags, conditional-kind data, saturating counter\nupdate, replacement initialization, old-data reads, and saved predictions.\nThe late target-alignment result must not feed these wide payload enables.\nAligned legal control transfers retain exactly the current training policy\nand timing; correctly predicted instructions gain no extra pipeline cycle.\n\nFor a train_control event, set valid_q[train_index] to train_install.\nAn aligned transfer installs the written entry. An uncacheable/misaligned\ntransfer may write raw payloads, but MUST clear that index'\"'s validity on\nthe same edge, even if it previously held another tag. This conservative\neviction is necessary because the payload was overwritten; leaving the\nunrelated old valid bit set would falsely validate the new tag/target.\nOnly this rare uncacheable-control collision changes allocation behavior.\nOrdinary and illegal instructions retain the current matching-full-tag\ninvalidation rule and must not overwrite or evict an unrelated entry.\nReset only validity as before; unreset payloads stay unobservable on misses.\nNever use payload allocation as permission to predict or execute a\nmisaligned target. EX architectural trap/alignment checks stay unchanged.\n\nKeep lookup gated by valid AND complete tag equality. Preserve exact\nfull-width saved predicted_next_pc for every accepted/queued instruction,\nand EX's comparison against the independently resolved architectural PC\nfor every advancing instruction. Corrective redirect remains immediate,\nwith priority over bus/decode holds and full occupancy. Preserve validity-\nonly decode flushing, wrong-path side-effect suppression, once-per-advance\ntraining, memory bounds, all RVFI fields, contiguous order, decoder default\nillegality, and both real/ALTOPS arithmetic implementations.\n\nExtend IF tests to explicitly drive the new control qualifier and prove\nthat an uncacheable control transfer clears validity after overwriting a\nsame-index different-tag entry. Cover aligned replacement and saturation,\nnot-taken branches with misaligned candidate targets, misaligned JALR,\nordinary/illegal matching and nonmatching invalidation, reset, simultaneous\nlookup/training, and saved queued predictions across overwritten payloads.\nUpdate the independent predictor model to distinguish payload allocation\nfrom entry visibility without removing any legality, retirement, queue,\ntrap, or wrong-path checks. Exercise older blocked memory operations,\nload-to-JALR forwarding, all queue occupancies, imem stalls, and MUL/DIV\nresponse edges. Run existing unit tests, unchanged single-channel formal\nand reference cosim gates, and canonical stalled CoreMark with CRC, UART,\nbounds, and timing-marker validation. Measure all three Gowin placements.\n\nThe forecast is six percent fitness gain, with low confidence until vendor\ntiming establishes the gain. CoreMark should preserve its 4,059,766\nbracketed cycles because its control targets are aligned. At that count,\nmedian Fmax must exceed approximately 59.163 MHz to exceed champion fitness\n139.32 by 4.6 percent. The unchanged divider and ALU/address paths can cap\nthe benefit, so select on measured Fmax times bracketed iterations/cycle.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Export train_control from decoded legality and control-transfer type, independently of forwarded operands or target alignment. Preserve existing train_valid, train_install, immediate recovery, and all architectural results.'},\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'Wire the additional internal EX-to-IF payload-allocation qualifier, preserving every top-level and RVFI port and existing pipeline connections.'},\n {'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'Write predictor payloads on valid control-transfer allocation, and separately gate entry visibility with existing target admissibility. Clear validity for any overwritten uncacheable-control index; retain matching-tag-only invalidation for ordinary/illegal instructions, old-data lookup, and saved queue predictions.'},\n {'file':'test/test_if_stage.py','description':'Drive the new qualifier explicitly and verify allocation/visibility separation, full-tag collisions followed by uncacheable control flow, alignment gating, reset, saturation, simultaneous updates, and immutable queued predictions.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Update the independent predictor model for conservative eviction on uncacheable control allocation, and add collision/misalignment tests with forwarded JALR operands and bus/arithmetic holds. Retain all exact retirement, trap, queue, and wrong-path side-effect checks.'}\n]}\ndef strings(dumper,value):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',value,style='|' if '\\\\n' in value else None)\nyaml.SafeDumper.add_representer(str,strings)\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint(f'Validated {p}')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_50", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport yaml, json, jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r7s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20260930-003-r7s2',\n'title':'Separate predictor payload allocation from target admissibility',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion already has a fully tagged 64-entry next-PC predictor and\ntwo-entry fetch queue. Earlier accuracy experiments show little remaining\ncycle headroom, and registering the complete training event reduced Fmax.\nCurrent vendor timing repeatedly crosses forwarding, EX, and IF table\nupdates: train_install includes target alignment derived from forwarded\nJALR operands and drives every tag, target, kind, and counter payload\nwrite enable. These payloads are harmless while their valid bit is clear,\nso their write enables need not wait for the late alignment decision.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Split predictor training into early payload allocation and late entry\nadmissibility, without delaying the training event or recovery. Preserve\nthe 64-entry fully tagged table, complete 30-bit aligned targets, current\ntwo-bit tagged direction policy, two-entry fall-through queue, arithmetic,\npipeline depth, and nret=1 ports. This is one predictor-update experiment.\n\nAdd an internal train_control signal from EX to IF, computed only from\nthe held decoded controls: \"'!in.ctrl.is_illegal AND (in.ctrl.is_branch OR\nin.ctrl.is_jump). Retain train_valid as the existing exactly-once valid\nEX-advance event qualified by reset, dmem freeze, and MUL/DIV completion.\nKeep train_install unchanged as the legal, aligned-target qualification.\n\nChange the tag/target/conditional/counter payload write enable to\n!reset AND train_valid AND train_control, rather than train_install.\nPreserve target data, full tags, conditional-kind data, saturating counter\nupdate, replacement initialization, old-data reads, and saved predictions.\nThe late target-alignment result must not feed these wide payload enables.\nAligned legal control transfers retain exactly the current training policy\nand timing; correctly predicted instructions gain no extra pipeline cycle.\n\nFor a train_control event, set valid_q[train_index] to train_install.\nAn aligned transfer installs the written entry. An uncacheable/misaligned\ntransfer may write raw payloads, but MUST clear that index'\"'s validity on\nthe same edge, even if it previously held another tag. This conservative\neviction is necessary because the payload was overwritten; leaving the\nunrelated old valid bit set would falsely validate the new tag/target.\nOnly this rare uncacheable-control collision changes allocation behavior.\nOrdinary and illegal instructions retain the current matching-full-tag\ninvalidation rule and must not overwrite or evict an unrelated entry.\nReset only validity as before; unreset payloads stay unobservable on misses.\nNever use payload allocation as permission to predict or execute a\nmisaligned target. EX architectural trap/alignment checks stay unchanged.\n\nKeep lookup gated by valid AND complete tag equality. Preserve exact\nfull-width saved predicted_next_pc for every accepted/queued instruction,\nand EX's comparison against the independently resolved architectural PC\nfor every advancing instruction. Corrective redirect remains immediate,\nwith priority over bus/decode holds and full occupancy. Preserve validity-\nonly decode flushing, wrong-path side-effect suppression, once-per-advance\ntraining, memory bounds, all RVFI fields, contiguous order, decoder default\nillegality, and both real/ALTOPS arithmetic implementations.\n\nExtend IF tests to explicitly drive the new control qualifier and prove\nthat an uncacheable control transfer clears validity after overwriting a\nsame-index different-tag entry. Cover aligned replacement and saturation,\nnot-taken branches with misaligned candidate targets, misaligned JALR,\nordinary/illegal matching and nonmatching invalidation, reset, simultaneous\nlookup/training, and saved queued predictions across overwritten payloads.\nUpdate the independent predictor model to distinguish payload allocation\nfrom entry visibility without removing any legality, retirement, queue,\ntrap, or wrong-path checks. Exercise older blocked memory operations,\nload-to-JALR forwarding, all queue occupancies, imem stalls, and MUL/DIV\nresponse edges. Run existing unit tests, unchanged single-channel formal\nand reference cosim gates, and canonical stalled CoreMark with CRC, UART,\nbounds, and timing-marker validation. Measure all three Gowin placements.\n\nThe forecast is six percent fitness gain, with low confidence until vendor\ntiming establishes the gain. CoreMark should preserve its 4,059,766\nbracketed cycles because its control targets are aligned. At that count,\nmedian Fmax must exceed approximately 59.163 MHz to exceed champion fitness\n139.32 by 4.6 percent. The unchanged divider and ALU/address paths can cap\nthe benefit, so select on measured Fmax times bracketed iterations/cycle.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Export train_control from decoded legality and control-transfer type, independently of forwarded operands or target alignment. Preserve existing train_valid, train_install, immediate recovery, and all architectural results.'},\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'Wire the additional internal EX-to-IF payload-allocation qualifier, preserving every top-level and RVFI port and existing pipeline connections.'},\n {'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'Write predictor payloads on valid control-transfer allocation, and separately gate entry visibility with existing target admissibility. Clear validity for any overwritten uncacheable-control index; retain matching-tag-only invalidation for ordinary/illegal instructions, old-data lookup, and saved queue predictions.'},\n {'file':'test/test_if_stage.py','description':'Drive the new qualifier explicitly and verify allocation/visibility separation, full-tag collisions followed by uncacheable control flow, alignment gating, reset, saturation, simultaneous updates, and immutable queued predictions.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Update the independent predictor model for conservative eviction on uncacheable control allocation, and add collision/misalignment tests with forwarded JALR operands and bus/arithmetic holds. Retain all exact retirement, trap, queue, and wrong-path side-effect checks.'}\n]}\ndef strings(dumper,value):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',value,style='|' if '\\\\n' in value else None)\nyaml.SafeDumper.add_representer(str,strings)\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint(f'Validated {p}')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Validated cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r7s2.yaml\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
