{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"agent_message","text":"The payload-enable change preserves CoreMark cycles but reduces Fmax, so I’ve rejected it. Registered recovery remains the strongest measured angle so far. I’m checking one final form that uses the existing EX/MEM architectural next-PC register to deliver corrections, with immediate younger squashing and no separate target register."}}
