utcome': 'regression', 'fitness': 125.16, 'fmax_mhz': 52.536, 'cycles': 4197517, 'critical_path': {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -14.899, 'arrival_ns': 25.193, 'logic_cells': 13, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}, 'implementation_notes': ''}\nKeep the existing 64-entry tagged target/direction predictor unchanged.\nChange only how its exact prediction is verified and how operand-\nindependent recovery PCs reach EX. In ID, compute sequential_candidate\n= fetch PC + 4 and direct_candidate = fetch PC + the existing decoded\nimmediate, using full 32-bit modulo arithmetic. Compare the fetch's\nexisting predicted_ne\n…[12530 of 15602 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4464ee77f3a9dfeb]…\ns, and MUL/DIV holds and\nresponse transfers; check exact retirement PCs/order and absence of\nwrong-path stores. Retain and run the existing unit suites and unchanged\nnret=1 formal and cosim gates. Measure canonical CRC/UART/bounds/marker-\nvalidated stalled CoreMark and all three Gowin placement options.\n\nThe forecast is a six-percent fitness gain primarily from reduced\npredictor-training routing and write-enable delay, with a small possible\ncycle cost from learning one cycle later. At unchanged champion cycles,\nmedian Fmax must exceed 56.47 MHz to beat fitness 132.98 by 4.6 percent;\nuse measured bracketed cycles to adjust that threshold. Prototype results\nmust establish the clock gain: moving the limiting path to the unchanged\ndivider or ALU is the main risk, so confidence is low until vendor timing.\n\nhyp-20260930-003-r7s2 Deliver prediction recovery from the registered EX/MEM next PC\n{'outcome': 'broken', 'fitness': None, 'fmax_mhz': None, 'cycles': None, 'critical_path': None, 'implementation_notes': None}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
