rom\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider/divisor_q_5_s0\",\n      \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider/remainder_q_13_s0\",\n      \"slack_ns\": -14.866,\n      \"arrival_ns\": 25.16,\n      \"logic_cells\": 23,\n      \"modules\": [\n        \"clock_ibuf\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_35", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nimport yaml\nimport jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r13s0.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261001-001-r13s0',\n'title':'Segmented borrow-lookahead subtractors for radix-4 division',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 200.89 iter/sec at median 81.557 MHz and 4,059,766 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its worst path traverses 67 cells inside the divider, from quotient state to response magnitude, at 17.757 ns arrival. Each of the two dependent radix-4 digits waits for full-width subtraction borrow flags. Round 12's digit-mux rewrite and fifteen-subtractor radix-16 expansion both regressed. Keep the successful recurrence and transaction timing, and shorten the subtractors themselves with shared local arithmetic and parallel block borrow propagation.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace only the three native 35-bit subtract/borrow calculations inside radix4_step with an exact segmented unsigned subtract34 helper. Apply it to both existing radix-4 digits. Preserve the 34-bit trial T={R,Q[31:30]}, exact registered D/2D/3D multiples, descending 3/2/1/0 priority selection and remainder mux. This is one arithmetic micro-optimization, with no extra registers or divide clocks.\n\nPartition each 34-bit input into eight low four-bit chunks and one high two-bit chunk. For low chunk j, compute an independent five-bit zero-borrow difference Z[j]={0,A_j}-{0,B_j}, local borrow generate G[j]=Z[j][4], and borrow propagate P[j]=(A_j==B_j). A chunk's outgoing borrow is G[j] OR (P[j] AND incoming_borrow). Calculate all low-chunk prefix borrows with explicit parallel prefix stages at distances 1,2,4: combine higher-range H and lower-range K as G=G_H OR (P_H AND G_K), P=P_H AND P_K. Each stage reads only the previous stage, never a serial updated accumulator. The initial incoming borrow is zero; chunk j>0 uses the prefix generate through chunk j-1.\n\nFor each low chunk, select Z[j][3:0] when its incoming borrow is zero, otherwise Z[j][3:0]-4'd1. Compute the high two-bit zero-borrow difference independently; use the low-32-bit prefix borrow for its local modulo-four decrement. The final borrow is high_generate OR (high_propagate AND low32_borrow). Return {final_borrow,complete_34_bit_difference}, exactly matching {1'b0,A}-{1'b0,B} modulo 2\"'^35. Keep decrements local to their four- or two-bit chunks; do not recreate a full-width correction adder. The explicit prefix should replace a full-width serial carry chain with short native chunk arithmetic, three small borrow-combine levels, and local result selection. It shares local differences with borrow generation instead of adding independent full-width comparator trees.\n\nUse the helper for diff1,diff2,diff3, leaving their high borrow-bit consumers and existing radix4_step control/data selection unchanged. Preserve first_step, second_step, the LUT-factored launch seed, seven iteration clocks, registered response magnitude/sign, conditional sign correction, divisor-zero behavior, INT_MIN/-1, request capture, held response and reset cancellation. Preserve every RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS formula and identical transaction timing. Keep the pipeline, final ID/EX operands, accepted-response bypass, predictor/fetch queue, load-use and bus holds, memory side effects, legality/alignment traps, nret=1 ports and exact RVFI values/order. No checker, wrapper, benchmark, contract or other core may change.\n\nProve the helper equivalent to native 35-bit subtraction for arbitrary 34-bit inputs without recurrence assumptions. Retain independent integer RV32M results and cycle-by-cycle seed/radix-4 state checks. Cover equality, generate/propagate/kill at every nibble boundary, long borrow runs, high bits of D/2D/3D, T=kD plus/minus one, every digit, zero divisors, all sign combinations and deterministic random full-width operands. Keep all existing latency, capture, response-hold, reset and ALTOPS assertions. Run unchanged unit/pipeline, formal including liveness, ISS cosim and canonical stalled CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/MMIO-marker validation.\n\nForecast eight percent higher fitness at unchanged CoreMark cycles. Acceptance requires fitness above 210.131 iter/sec and median Fmax above approximately 85.309 MHz at the current cycle count. Prefix routing, chunk mux/decrement cost and the ordinary EX address path can limit the gain; judge all three Gowin placement options rather than cell count. An isolated helper SAT miter has already proved exact 35-bit equivalence for arbitrary inputs; vendor timing and whole-core correctness remain implementation requirements.'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/divider.sv','description':'''Implement an exact 34-bit segmented subtraction helper returning its 35-bit difference/borrow. Use eight four-bit low chunks, a two-bit high chunk, parallel distance-1/2/4 borrow-prefix stages and local conditional decrements. Substitute only the three subtraction expressions in radix4_step; preserve all selection, seed, state, latency, sign, handshake and ALTOPS behavior.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'''Extend independent RV32M and existing intermediate-state checks with nibble-boundary borrow generate/propagate/kill, long borrow chains, all-digit threshold equality and neighboring values, high divisor-multiple bits and signed/zero boundaries. Keep every arithmetic, exact-latency, capture, response-hold, reset and real/ALTOPS check intact.'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=88,default_flow_style=False))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Revised hypothesis written; schema valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
