{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('round_id',0)>=8 and d.get('category')=='micro_opt':\n  print(d['id'],d['title'],d.get('delta_pct'))\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print(h.get('hypothesis',h) if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20260930-001-r8s0 Parallel carry-consistency checking for JALR prediction verification -0.37\nReplace only the JALR prediction-match comparator in ex_stage.sv with a parallel local carry-consistency check. Keep the existing full 32-bit rs1+immediate adder and cleared-bit real target, every pipeline register, operand source, predictor entry and policy, immediate redirect/training timing, queue and arithmetic latency. This is one combinational micro-optimization: verify the predicted sum without waiting for the real sum's carry chain.\n\nLet A be the actual forwarded rs1, B the existing immediate, and P the exact saved predicted_next_pc. Compute bitwise propagate X=A XOR B and generate G=A AND B. For significant bits i=1..31 infer the only carry-in consistent with the predicted sum bit: C[i]=X[i] XOR P[i]. A JALR prediction matches exactly iff P[0]=0, C[1]=G[0], and every i=1..30 satisfies C[i+1]=G[i] OR (X[i] AND C[i]). Implement the thirty latter constraints as one vector equality, C[31:2] == (G[30:1] | (X[30:1] & C[30:1])), combined with the two low-bit conditions. Each bit's constraint is independent combinational logic and the reduction is balanced. Do not implement this as a serial carry recurrence. The identity follows by induction from the genuine zero carry into bit zero; carry-out of bit 31 is discarded because addition is modulo 2^32.\n\nBit zero of the actual sum is intentionally ignored because JALR clears it, but its carry into bit one is still A[0] AND B[0]. Requiring P[0]=0 preserves complete equality to {jalr_sum[31:1],1'b0}; all 31 higher predicted bits participate. No address bits may be narrowed to the benchmark range. Retain native jalr_sum=A+B for redirect_target, predictor training, alignment checking and architectural pc_next. Never substitute a predicted target for the real target. The verification and target arithmetic now settle in parallel instead of a full-width equality waiting behind the adder.\n\nPreserve the existing misaligned-JALR target-bit-one trap, link-write suppression and seque\n…[20522 of 23594 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4e817c932d3ec0d1]…\nV32M results and cycle-by-cycle seed/radix-4 state checks. Cover equality, generate/propagate/kill at every nibble boundary, long borrow runs, high bits of D/2D/3D, T=kD plus/minus one, every digit, zero divisors, all sign combinations and deterministic random full-width operands. Keep all existing latency, capture, response-hold, reset and ALTOPS assertions. Run unchanged unit/pipeline, formal including liveness, ISS cosim and canonical stalled CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/MMIO-marker validation.\n\nForecast eight percent higher fitness at unchanged CoreMark cycles. Acceptance requires fitness above 210.131 iter/sec and median Fmax above approximately 85.309 MHz at the current cycle count. Prefix routing, chunk mux/decrement cost and the ordinary EX address path can limit the gain; judge all three Gowin placement options rather than cell count. An isolated helper SAT miter has already proved exact 35-bit equivalence for arbitrary inputs; vendor timing and whole-core correctness remain implementation requirements.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
