 req_ready must continue to exclude busy and pending responses. Keep\n  launch capture, LUT-factored seed, exact D/2D/3D widths, both native\n  radix-4 steps, descending priority selection, seven iteration edges,\n  reset cancellation, divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 semantics unchan\n…[1412 of 4484 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5882233d0edbd664]…\nhanged CoreMark cycles,\n  with low confidence pending all three Gowin placement options.\n  Acceptance requires more than 210.131 iter/sec and approximately\n  85.309 MHz at 4,059,766 bracketed cycles. No gain is claimed measured.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/divider.sv\n    description: |\n      Remove redundant real response-magnitude storage and use the held\n      final quotient/remainder recurrence registers as response storage.\n      Select the captured operation's magnitude after those registers.\n      Preserve every arithmetic step, sign rule, state boundary, latency,\n      handshake, reset behavior and exact ALTOPS substitution.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve existing independent arithmetic, recurrence and latency\n      checks. Extend response-hold cases to verify completed recurrence\n      banks and results remain stable despite input changes, including\n      every DIV/REM signedness, zero divisor, overflow and reset case.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
