{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\":\\\\s*\\\"structural\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260930-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Move division out of the combinational execute path\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The only recorded bench experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12,\\nmedian Fmax 5.442 MHz, and a 199.837 ns path through forwarding and\\nu_ex/u_alu with 156 cells. No LESSONS.md or earlier structural attempts\\nexist in this fixture. The ALU implements signed and unsigned division\\nand remainder with combinational / and % operators. These are likely\\nresponsible for the very deep arithmetic path; even instructions that\\ndo not divide must meet the clock constraint imposed by that hardware.\\nMoving this arithmetic behind registers should substantially improve\\nFmax, at the cost of additional cycles only for DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only recorded bench experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12,\\nmedian Fmax 5.442 MHz, and a 199.837 ns path through forwarding and\\nu_ex/u_alu with 156 cells. No LESSONS.md or earlier structural attempts\\nexist in this fixture. The ALU implements signed and unsigned division\\nand remainder with combinational / and % operators. These are likely\\nresponsible for the very deep arithmetic path; even instructions that\\ndo not divide must meet the clock constraint imposed by that hardware.\\nMoving this arithmetic behind registers should substantially improve\\nFmax, at the cost of additional cycles only for DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational divide/remainder cone with one shared,\\nblocking, registered divider in EX. Use unsigned restoring division\\nwith four explicitly bounded quotient-bit steps per clock, eight\\niteration clocks, operand magnitude capture at launch, and signed\\ncorrection on completion. Target at most ten EX clocks from accepting\\na request to transferring its result under zero-wait memory, and at\\nmost ten clocks between successive retirements for back-to-back divide\\ninstructions. This keeps progress inside the existing formal liveness\\nwindow without changing any checker. Each\n…[126430 of 129502 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f4ca290021f565f2]…\n \"vs_baseline\": 1451.4, \"fmax_mhz\": 76.337, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4059766, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5715, \"ff\": 2126, \"seeds\": [74.303, 76.337, 76.337], \"perturbations\": [[0, 74.303, 11], [1, 76.337, 12], [2, 76.337, 12]], \"lutram\": 24, \"bsram\": 7, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.ctrl.is_auipc_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -8.458, \"arrival_ns\": 18.753, \"logic_cells\": 15, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 11, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-30T23:04:25.153690Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 12, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-01 hyp-20260930-002-r12s1 (regression, -6.40%): Fifteen parallel 37-bit subtractors and a balanced 16-way remainder OR tree cut divider path cells from 67 to 39 but increased its delay and exposed EX-to-dmem timing, showing that reduced serial depth alone does not guarantee higher Gowin Fmax at unchanged CoreMark cycles.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
