{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nrows=[json.loads(s) for s in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]\nfor x in rows:\n if x.get('category')=='structural':\n  h=x.get('hypothesis',{})\n  s=h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h\n  print('\\\\nID',x['id'],'TITLE',x['title'],'OUTCOME',x.get('outcome'),'DELTA',x.get('delta_pct'),'FMAX',x.get('fmax_mhz'),'CYCLES',x.get('cycles'))\n  print('PROPOSAL',s[:1800])\n  print('PATH',x.get('critical_path'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\nID hyp-20260930-002-r1s1 TITLE Move division out of the combinational execute path OUTCOME improvement DELTA 609.08 FMAX 38.602 CYCLES 4491485\nPROPOSAL Replace the combinational divide/remainder cone with one shared,\nblocking, registered divider in EX. Use unsigned restoring division\nwith four explicitly bounded quotient-bit steps per clock, eight\niteration clocks, operand magnitude capture at launch, and signed\ncorrection on completion. Target at most ten EX clocks from accepting\na request to transferring its result under zero-wait memory, and at\nmost ten clocks between successive retirements for back-to-back divide\ninstructions. This keeps progress inside the existing formal liveness\nwindow without changing any checker. Each iteration uses a 33-bit\npartial remainder and subtract/borrow selection; do not infer / or %\nor unroll all 32 quotient steps into a single combinational path.\nPreserve single-cycle execution of every other ALU operation, including\nthe existing multipliers, to make this one divider-focused structural\nchange. A four-step iteration is a timing/latency compromise that cuts\nthe division depth by roughly eight while bounding the retirement gap.\n\nLaunch only for a valid, legal division instruction whose older MEM\ninstruction can advance. Capture both fully forwarded source operands,\nthe operation, and the instruction's RVFI source values exactly once.\nHold fetch and ID/EX while division is pending. Allow older EX/MEM and\nMEM/WB instructions to drain: inject an invalid EX/MEM bubble with\nside-effect controls cleared whenever the divider cannot transfer,\nrather than repeatedly holding and reissuing the older memory operation.\nExisting data-memory backpressure still holds an unaccepted memory\nrequest and clears only MEM/WB valid as required for forwarding.\nHold a completed divider response until EX/MEM accepts it; consume it\nexactly once, then resume normal EX/MEM forwarding to dependent users.\nGate redire\nPATH {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider/remainder_q_5_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack\n…[27432 of 30504 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:afc711505066bcd4]…\nes, shifters, bitwise logic and\nsign correction on their existing implementation.\n\nExtract each current radix4_step into a combinational module so three\nhard subtractors can operate concurrently. Zero-extend its 34-bit\ntrial X and registered divisor multiple Y to 54 bits and use\nDOUT[34:0] as the original 35-bit difference. Because X,Y are below\n2^34, these low bits exactly match zero-extended 35-bit subtraction;\nbit 34 is the borrow flag. Preserve high multiple bits when 3D\nexceeds 2^32, descending 3/2/1/0 digit selection and low-32-bit\nremainder selection verbatim. Connect the two digit modules in the\ncurrent order and retain the existing iteration registers.\n\nKeep the four-bit LUT seed, registered D/2D/3D, seven iterations,\nquotient/remainder state, registered response magnitude and sign\ncorrection\nPATH {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_val_21_s0', 'to': 'dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -8.01, 'arrival_ns': 18.305, 'logic_cells': 11, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
