ause the prediction actually used travels with the fetch.\n\nCarry the selected predicted next PC in if_id_t and id_ex_t. When a fetch\nis actually accepted into ID/EX, advance the PC to that prediction; hold\nthe PC and prediction payload appropriately during load-use and data-bus\nstalls. Prediction itself must neither suppress the fetched instruction\nnor flush ID. In EX compute the architecturally resolved next PC using\nthe existing forwarded operands and misalignment/trap behavior. Compare\nit with the saved predicted next PC for EVERY valid instruction, including\nordinary instructions and illegal encodings. Issue a corrective redirect\nand squash the younger fetch only when these next PCs differ. Correctly\npredicted taken transfers therefore captu\n…[38439 of 41511 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b7446e0bf48eb37f]…\nJALR sum for resolved_next_pc, corrective target, jump\nlink values, target alignment checks, predictor training and RVFI.\nA prediction must never replace architectural arithmetic. Preserve\nequality even when direct and sequential targets coincide, when\npredictions differ only in high bits, and when stale table entries\nnow fetch ordinary, illegal, misaligned or blocking M instructions.\n\nThis is one predictor-verification timing change, with no new pipeline\nfield, table organization, prediction policy or recovery bubble.\nPreserve once-per-advance training, old-data lookup, immutable queued\npredictions, validity-only younger squash, redirect priority, bus\nbackpressure, load-use bubbling, complete decode operand bypass,\nMUL/DIV capture/hold/response behavior and real/ALTOPS arithmetic.\nPreserve nret=1 ports, architectural RVFI values, contiguous order,\nforward progress, decoder legality and every memory/CRC/UART/marker\ninvariant. No evaluation file, formal bound or checker may change.\n\nTest the three mat\nNOTES: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
