{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_40", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-003-r13s2.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261001-003-r13s2',\n'title':'Compress next-PC tags and targets with one shared code-region prefix',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 200.89 iter/sec at 81.557 MHz and 4,059,766\nbracketed CoreMark cycles. Prior table banking added selection and routing\nand lost Fmax; carry-consistency verification left the divider critical.\nThe return stack saved just 2,196 cycles. A new trace probe of the unchanged\nchampion reproduced the canonical CRCs and exactly 4,059,766 cycles. Its\nretirement-order model counted 62,551 next-PC errors, and a 256-entry gshare\nmodel made 74,566 errors, so direction accuracy has little demonstrated\nfitness headroom. The current predictor instead redundantly stores the\nsame upper code-address bits in every full tag and every target. Sharing\nthose bits can remove substantial predictor storage and routing without\nchanging predictions for code contained in one 64 KiB region.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace the predictor's full per-entry tag/target representation with\none shared 16-bit source code-region prefix and a 64-entry region-local\nnext-PC table. This is a single predictor storage compression experiment.\nKeep the same 64 logical entries, PC[7:2] index, two-bit direction policy,\nimmediate EX training/recovery, two-entry fall-through queue, pipeline\nstages, arithmetic, decoder and nret=1 interface. Do not add banking,\nhistory, a return stack, target arithmetic on lookup or another predictor.\n\nStore region_q = source PC[31:16] once. Each entry stores the eight-bit\nsource tag PC[15:8], fourteen-bit aligned target[15:2], valid, conditional\nkind and the existing two-bit saturating counter. A hit requires BOTH\npc[31:16] == region_q and a valid matching eight-bit row tag. Thus region,\nrow tag and index together still identify the complete aligned 32-bit PC;\nthis is a factorization of the full tag, not partial-tag aliasing. Compute\nthe shared region equality in parallel with the unchanged asynchronous\nrow lookup. On a predicted-taken hit reconstruct the complete target as\n{pc[31:16], target_low[13:0], 2'b00}; otherwise use the original PC+4.\nNo adder, bank-selection mux or truncated architectural PC is introduced.\n\nCache only transfers whose existing train_install is true AND whose\nresolved train_target[31:16] equals train_pc[31:16]. All architectural\ncontrol transfers still execute and recover normally. A cross-region\ntarget is uncacheable and fetches sequentially until the existing EX\ncorrection redirects it; never silently truncate or substitute its target.\nKeep independently resolved full-width EX targets, exact saved prediction\ncomparisons for EVERY advancing instruction, and real RVFI next PCs.\n\nOn each existing train_valid && train_install event, write the narrow\nrow payload using the ORIGINAL payload write enable. Do not put the new\nregion-target equality into the tag/target/kind/counter memory write\nenables. Set that row's valid bit to the same-region-target equality;\nan uncacheable transfer clears its row so an overwritten payload cannot\nremain visible under an older entry. If train_pc's source region differs\nfrom region_q, change region_q and clear ALL old row valid bits on that\nsame edge before setting only the new row's eligible valid bit. Perform\nthis source-region switch even if that particular target is uncacheable.\nOther row payloads remain unreset and hidden by validity. Reset clears\nvalidity and initializes the shared prefix. Ordinary, illegal and other\nnoninstall events retain matching-full-PC invalidation only, including\nthe shared region match; they cannot evict an unrelated source region.\n\nFor conditional counter training, train_match must include the pre-edge\nshared region match, row validity and low tag. Preserve saturation on a\nmatching conditional entry and weak initialization on replacement or\nchanged kind. A source-region switch always initializes the new row,\nregardless of equal low tags. Use pre-edge state on simultaneous lookup\nand update and preserve every accepted fetch's exact full-width prediction\nthrough queue residence and ID/EX holds. A later region switch, row update\nor invalidation must never recompute an already accepted prediction.\n\nThe entry payload shrinks from 57 to 25 bits, plus one shared 16-bit\nprefix: total predictor state including valid bits falls from 3,712 to\n1,680 bits. The main timing opportunity is narrower memory outputs and\nremoval of sixteen upper tag/target bits from each row, with the shared\nregion compare running before/alongside lookup. This differs from failed\nshallow banking because it preserves one table and adds no selection\nlevel. Preserve original payload enable timing so compression does not\ncreate a late full-target-to-wide-memory-enable cone. Cross-region\ntraining's validity/prefix path still needs actual vendor timing.\n\nPreserve all existing advance qualification, correction priority over\nbus/decode holds and queue fullness, validity-only younger squash,\nload-use bubbling, complete operand capture/bypass, MUL/DIV request and\nresponse timing, real/ALTOPS arithmetic, exactly-once memory side effects,\ntrap/alignment behavior, contiguous channel-0 retirement and liveness.\nDo not alter any checker, wrapper, benchmark or evaluation contract.\n\nExtend the independent IF predictor model to this representation. Check\nall 64 rows, saturation and changed kinds; source PCs with equal low tags\nbut different upper sixteen bits; local versus cross-region branch,\nJAL and changing JALR targets; uncacheable payload overwrite; matching\nand nonmatching ordinary invalidation; region changes concurrent with\nlookup/queue transfers; reset; and predictions queued before a region\nchange. Include legal high-address synthetic IF tests without changing\nthe execution memory bounds. At pipeline level use distinct source\nregions within the legal one-MiB RAM, exercise control/data hazards and\nindependent imem/dmem stalls, and check exact retired PCs and absence of\nwrong-path stores. Retain existing decoder/ALU/pipeline assertions.\n\nRun unchanged nret=1 formal including liveness, reference cosim and\ncanonical stalled CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/start-stop validation. The\nprototype must preserve 4,059,766 bracketed CoreMark cycles before a clock\ngain is credited. Score all three Gowin placement options: at unchanged\ncycles, acceptance requires median Fmax above approximately 85.309 MHz\nand fitness above 210.131 iter/sec. Forecast six percent higher fitness;\nconfidence remains low because the unchanged divider may still limit\nFmax and code spanning several regions will pay extra target misses.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'''Factor full source tags into one shared 16-bit region and eight-bit\nrow tags; store fourteen-bit local targets and reconstruct only on a\nfull-identity hit. Add same-region target eligibility and atomic source\nregion replacement/validity clearing while preserving original payload\nwrite enables, counters, queue semantics and exact saved predictions.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_if_stage.py','description':'''Extend the independent predictor/queue reference model for region-local\nstorage, full-PC hit identity, cross-region targets, source region switches,\nhidden uncacheable writes, old-data training and queued predictions.\nPreserve every existing transfer, counter, recovery and reset assertion.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Exercise calls, branches and JALR between separate legal RAM regions,\nreturning to earlier regions under load hazards and independent bus stalls.\nVerify complete retired PCs, contiguous orders and exactly-once effects;\nretain canonical predictor, arithmetic, trap and wrong-path-store checks.\n'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,default_flow_style=False,width=80))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Revised hypothesis validates:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
