{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_61", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-003-r13s2.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261001-003-r13s2',\n'title':'Update the tagged next-PC predictor only for control-flow instructions',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 200.89 iter/sec at 81.557 MHz and 4,059,766\nbracketed CoreMark cycles. Banking, delayed training and carry-consistency\nverification have lost Fmax; a return stack saved only 2,196 cycles.\nA new unchanged-champion trace reproduced the canonical CRCs and exactly\n4,059,766 cycles. Its retirement-order model found little direction\naccuracy headroom, and a 256-entry gshare model increased errors. Predictor\ncompression, smaller tables, index hashing and a registered queue also\nlost vendor Fmax in exploratory probes. The current target table still\nreceives a qualified event for EVERY advancing instruction, including\nblocking M responses, solely to invalidate matching entries on ordinary\ninstructions. Exact saved-next-PC verification already repairs stale\npredictions independently of this invalidation. Removing that maintenance\npath can simplify the predictor's validity and update controls.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Make the existing 64-entry, fully tagged next-PC table update only on\nvalid legal control-flow instructions. This is one predictor-maintenance\narchitecture experiment. Keep the original table capacity, index, complete\nPC tags and thirty-bit aligned targets, conditional kind, two-bit counters,\nimmediate training and correction, two-entry fall-through queue, pipeline\nstages, arithmetic and nret=1 top-level interface. Do not combine this\nwith banking, compression, history, hashing or a new recovery stage.\n\nStop invalidating a matching table entry when EX advances an ordinary,\nillegal, or uncacheable instruction. Valid bits become allocate-only:\nreset clears them, and a qualified legal aligned control transfer sets\nits indexed valid bit and writes/replaces that row's normal payload.\nUncacheable transfers do not overwrite a row. A full-tag stale entry may\ntherefore remain present until a later cacheable control transfer replaces\nit. This changes predictor policy, never architectural execution. EX must\ncontinue comparing EVERY advancing instruction's exact saved predicted\nnext PC with its independently computed architectural next PC, including\nordinary, illegal, misaligned, MUL and DIV instructions. A stale hit is\ncorrected and younger work is squashed before it can cause side effects.\nA stale ordinary instruction may pay a repeated correction bubble, but\nstill advances and retires; never suppress recovery to justify the policy.\n\nReplace train_valid = generic ex_advance with a dedicated early control-\nflow training event based on registered in.valid, validated nonillegal\nbranch-or-jump kind, \"'!stall, !reset and no pending MUL/DIV transaction.\nFor reachable core states, a decoded control transfer cannot also be an\nM operation, so this event equals generic ex_advance for control flow\nwithout depending on div_hold/mul_hold response-ready logic. Retain\npending-transaction guards to reject unrelated inputs during an owned\nM transaction. Prove/check equivalence to generic EX advance qualified\nby legal control-flow kind for actual core instruction transfers. Do not\nuse the dedicated event for redirect, retirement, EX/MEM advancement,\noperand bypass or arithmetic request/response ownership: those retain\ntheir exact current qualification.\n\nKeep train_install'\"'s current full legality and target-alignment checks.\nBoth valid-bit allocation and tag/target/kind/counter writes occur only\non the dedicated training event AND train_install. A not-taken branch\nwith a misaligned candidate remains uncacheable. Keep pre-edge full-tag\ntraining matches for conditional counter saturation and weak initialization\non replacement/changed kind. Eliminating ordinary invalidation removes\nthe wide training-tag comparison from validity maintenance; the match\nstill serves counter learning. Reset only existing validity bits, leave\npayload arrays unreset, and retain original compact memory inference.\nThere is no training-to-lookup bypass and no delayed training register.\n\nKeep simultaneous lookup/update old-data semantics and preserve every\naccepted fetch's exact prediction through queue residence and ID/EX holds.\nReplacement or later instruction changes cannot retroactively recompute\na prediction. Preserve correction priority over queue fullness, imem\nbackpressure and younger hazards, validity-only squash, load-use bubbles,\ncomplete decode operand delivery, saved M payloads, stable M responses,\nall alignment/decoder traps, real RVFI PCs and values, contiguous single-\nchannel order, exactly-once memory side effects and symbolic progress.\nDo not alter any checker, wrapper, benchmark or evaluation contract.\n\nUpdate the independent IF predictor model for allocate-only validity.\nKeep all counter, replacement, old-data, queue, reset and recovery checks;\npolicy-specific assertions should expect a stale matching row to remain\nrather than expect invalidation. Add pipeline tests that first populate\na row, then present ordinary, illegal, misaligned and blocking M code at\nthe same PC. Verify exact linear/resolved next-PC recovery, complete\nretirement fields, no wrong-path stores and forward progress even when\nthe stale row survives multiple visits. Exercise changing JALR targets,\nfull-tag collisions, imem/dmem stalls, load-to-control dependencies,\nM launch/hold/accepted-response edges and reset cancellation. Check that\nonly actual advancing cacheable control transfers train and none repeat\nwhile EX is held. Keep all invariant-enforcing assertions unchanged.\n\nRun unchanged nret=1 formal including liveness, reference cosim and\ncanonical stalled CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/start-stop checks. For immutable\nCoreMark code, matching ordinary invalidation should never be needed,\nso the candidate should retain 4,059,766 bracketed cycles. Measure all\nthree Gowin placements; at unchanged cycles acceptance requires median\nFmax above approximately 85.309 MHz and fitness above 210.131 iter/sec.\nForecast six percent more fitness from simpler update qualification and\nvalidity control. Confidence is low: unchanged divider/address paths may\nremain limiting, and self-modifying or symbolic code may incur additional\ncorrections without compromising correctness or forward progress.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Generate a dedicated once-per-advance legal control-flow training event\nfrom registered kind/validity and pipeline ownership, eliminating blocking\nM response-ready logic from predictor maintenance. Preserve generic\nadvance for all architectural, recovery, bypass and arithmetic behavior.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'''Remove matching ordinary/illegal/uncacheable invalidation and update\nvalidity only on reset or qualified legal aligned control-flow allocation.\nPreserve full tags/targets, memory organization, counter learning, exact\nsaved predictions, immediate recovery and the fall-through fetch queue.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_if_stage.py','description':'''Model allocate-only row validity while retaining all independent counter,\nreplacement, old-data, queue and reset checks. Verify stale full-tag rows\nremain visible until replacement and never change saved predictions.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_ex_stage.py','description':'''Check dedicated training-event ownership and equivalence on actual legal\ncontrol-flow advances, including stalls, reset and pending M operations;\nretain all resolution, trap, bypass and arithmetic handshake assertions.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Verify stale-entry correction and forward progress when populated PCs\nlater hold ordinary, illegal, misaligned and blocking M instructions.\nExercise hazards and independent bus stalls; retain exact RVFI retirement,\norder and wrong-path-store checks without weakening any hard invariant.\n'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=80))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert h['id']=='hyp-20261001-003-r13s2' and h['category']=='predictor'\nprint('Complete hypothesis validates:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
