n a valid tag hit, predict the cached target for\nan unconditional transfer or a conditional branch whose counter MSB is 1;\notherwise predict PC+4. This predicts JAL/JALR as well as conditional\nbranches through the same table; do not add another predictor mechanism.\nKeep the implementation small and reset only entry-valid bits, allowing\ntag/target/counter storage to infer compact memory where supported. Read\nthe old entry on simultaneous lookup/training; no EX-to-IF table bypass\nis necessary because the prediction actually used travels with the fetch.\n\nCarry the selected predicted next PC in if_id_t and id_ex_t. When a fetch\nis actually accepted into ID/EX, advance the PC to that prediction; hold\nthe PC and prediction payload appropriately during load-use and data-bus\nstalls. Prediction itself\n…[58529 of 61601 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:67f85d05b1b2e5c9]…\nkind/counter writes occur only\non the dedicated training event AND train_install. A not-taken branch\nwith a misaligned candidate remains uncacheable. Keep pre-edge full-tag\ntraining matches for conditional counter saturation and weak initialization\non replacement/changed kind. Eliminating ordinary invalidation removes\nthe wide training-tag comparison from validity maintenance; the match\nstill serves counter learning. Reset only existing validity bits, leave\npayload arrays unreset, and retain original compact memory inference.\nThere is no training-to-lookup bypass and no delayed training register.\n\nKeep simultaneous lookup/update old-data semantics and preserve every\naccepted fetch's exact prediction through queue residence and ID/EX holds.\nReplacement or later instruction changes cannot retroactively recompute\na prediction. Preserve correction priority over queue fullness, imem\nbackpressure and younger hazards, validity-only squash, load-use bubbles,\ncomplete decode operand delivery, saved M payloads, stable\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
