{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,pathlib\nfor l in pathlib.Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d.get('category')=='predictor':\n  print(d['id'],d['title'],d['outcome'],d.get('fmax_mhz'),d.get('cycles'))\n  if '-r8s2' in d['id'] or '-r9s2' in d['id'] or '-r7s2' in d['id'] or '-r6s2' in d['id']:\n   h=d['hypothesis'];print(h['motivation']);print(h['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20260930-003-r1s2 Small tagged next-PC predictor removes taken-control bubbles regression 5.393 4208674\nhyp-20260930-003-r2s2 64-entry next-PC prediction on the registered-divider champion regression 38.64 4197517\nhyp-20260930-003-r3s2 64-entry next-PC predictor with validity-only recovery improvement 49.426 4197517\nhyp-20260930-003-r4s2 Precompute predictor recovery candidates before execute regression 52.536 4197517\nhyp-20260930-003-r5s2 Two-entry predicted-path lookahead hides instruction stalls improvement 53.987 4059766\nhyp-20260930-003-r6s2 Register EX predictor training before table updates regression 51.1 4059766\nThe champion already has a 64-entry fully tagged next-PC predictor and\ntwo-entry fetch lookahead. Earlier doubling from 32 to 64 entries saved\nonly 11,157 cycles, while a retired-stream profile of the canonical run\nsuggests little further benefit from a return stack or a small history\npredictor. A compact-target prototype also preserved 4,059,766 bracketed\ncycles but reduced median Gowin Fmax to 47.778 MHz. Its worst paths expose\nthe long forwarded-operand-to-predictor-update chain: EX branch/JALR\nresolution and alignment checks feed IF table write enables directly.\nDecoupling predictor learning from EX should reduce this fanout without\nadding latency to architectural branch recovery or changing arithmetic.\n\nAdd exactly one clocked predictor-training event register between the\nexisting EX outputs and IF inputs, preferably in core.sv. Retain the\ncurrent 64-entry table, complete tags and thirty-bit targets, direction\npolicy, two-entry fetch queue, pipeline depth, and all arithmetic. The\nonly architectural change is that predictor training arrives in IF one\ncycle after the corresponding valid EX advance instead of driving table\nupdate logic combinationally from that advance.\n\nRegister all six existing training fields together: train_valid,\ntrain_pc[31:0], train_target[31:0], train_install, train_conditional,\nand train_taken. Connect IF to these registered signals while leaving\nEX connected to it\n…[16834 of 19906 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7292f8b56de05a13]…\nnspect Gowin's tag/target\nwrite-enable cones to confirm alignment and M-response controls were\nremoved. Measure all three placement options and bracketed cycles.\n\nForecast six percent higher fitness with little resource overhead.\nConfidence is low until vendor timing shows sufficient benefit despite\nimmediate recovery remaining combinational. At unchanged 4,059,766\ncycles, acceptance requires median Fmax above approximately 75.442 MHz\nand fitness above 185.832 iter/sec. Do not change any evaluation file,\nformal bound, decoder legality rule, arithmetic timing or external port.\n\nhyp-20260930-003-r10s2 Resolve-trained return stack for multi-caller functions regression 76.885 4057570\nhyp-20260930-003-r11s2 Eight shallow banks for the 64-entry next-PC predictor regression 70.398 4059766\nhyp-20260930-003-r12s2 Parallel carry-consistency verification of predicted next PCs regression 78.489 4059766\nhyp-20261001-003-r13s2 Update the tagged next-PC predictor only for control-flow instructions regression 82.457 4059766\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
